ike this TM, which no one's bothered to claim."0Honestly, just take it. Make my job easier."6They don't pay me enough to deal with this stuff."FI've been hired to assist in acquiring specific Pokemon to study."UIt involves me going around the local battling scene to find the right trainers."ZMost of them accept since it's easy cash, though some of them help for other reasons."^Some like the idea of contributing to science, others are looking to build their resumes."Some are just bored!">Take this is a token of appreciation for checking us out."*Feel free to contribute how you want."5There are rewards for doing so, but no pressure!"KIf you want to join a study, visit the 2nd floor of the main building."bThe computer lab here is nice, it lets me use the internet to search for all sorts of things."AIt makes me wonder how people did stuff before the internet.""Science must have been tough."Anyways, check this out."*dink*"See how easy that was?"PAren't computers rad? With enough work, it seems like they can do anything!"MOf course, learning how to make them do what we want is the hard part...";Helena, the gym leader, is one of the executives here."IShe's in charge of the logistics and funding for LuxTech's projects."BShe used to do the same thing for Team Chasm back in the day."KTalk about previous work experience. Her resume must have been killer."	Ugh.""I wanted to interview Helena."�She's the local gym leader and LuxTech's local, uh, advisor. We figured coming to her workplace might make the  easier to pull off."KShe said we'd have a 15 minute time frame to get a recorded interview."@Instead she sends us some intern with pre-recorded answers."Very disappointing."KWe host a Porygon on our local network to help with file organization."2Huh, I wonder what it's like being a Porygon."aI can't even begin to fathom what travelling through the net like that would even feel like."-You could be anywhere, anytime, at will."..."'I should clear my browser history."SThey had my Pokemon do a lot of battling the other day. You know, for science."5It was a ton of fun, but it was also exhausting."*I gotta make sure we don't overdo it."`We're here on correspondence about LuxTech's sponsorship of the upcoming League Tournament."~The employees here must have all gotten some basic media training. Lot's of them were comfortable in front of the camera."7LuxTech must put a lot of effort into their image.""Some even gave me free stuff."XYou should take some of it off me, though, cause my equipment already weighs a ton!"iI'll talk with my co-worker once we get home. We can probably stitch together something interesting."6Ah, good news? Excellent! Hand over the shipment."%You give the shipment to Helena."WThis sets us a few days ahead of schedule -- well, ahead of the adjusted schedule.":Regardless, I will uphold my end of this transaction."EMeet me in my gym when you’re ready. And do try and be prompt."�No, I don’t have anything better to do than wait here for someone to get my shipment back from wherever in the caves it ended up."8I mean, I have a phone. Ever heard of a video call?"Despite almost no language expression abilities, Pokemon actually have significantly better language comprehension than humans.";I've taught my Kadabra here multiple coding languages."RHe's the perfect "Rubber Ducklett", catching mistakes as soon as I type them!"'Hey, are you \PN? Mavis’s child?"8I haven’t seen you since you were Munchlax-sized."9Oh, excuse me, were you registering for a challenge?"�We’re processing all the latecomers trying to get into the Championships, plus logistics for the event itself, so -- actually."&You’re chasing Zain, I presume?"9Of course. I lost to him, oh, a week and a half ago?"YI understand that rivalry -- and I understand you don’t have a few weeks to spare."VJust like I don’t have time to wait for a particularly late shipment to arrive."[Normally I’d praise you for playing your cards close to your chest, but not with me."cDon’t pla