keep looking."/Ah, you had me excited there for a moment."-A Chingling! Alright, let's get started!"%\PN traded Chingling for Grimer!"Wow, it's so adorable!">The beautiful sounds my Chingling makes... ah, I love it!"No"YesIu;␀�-[[S"[In order to fight the climate, you have to keep you and your Pokemon in tip-top shape."WBoth physically and mentally. Out there, your body and your mind are under attack."CHaving one crack will lead to the other cracking just as fast."Take this."aUse it if it helps, but the most important part is that a perfect body needs a perfect mind."hIf you ever get tired of battling and want a change of pace, we're always looking for new recruits."dWe're doing operations all over the region, so you'll get to see everything Makya has to offer."II help coordinate rescue operations with some of the Makyan rangers."�We used to just work around the Ice Cave area, but now we've been funded by LuxTech to start holding operations for the entire region."It's been tough."8Strange Pokemon have been appearing out of nowhere."AA lot of Mayka's caverns have been deemed unsafe for travel."WWe manage, but if people would stop being so reckless, that would also help a ton."&The mountains here are dangerous."dWinding tunnels, dead ends, and circular paths make it a labyrinth even for experienced hikers."_Now all of a sudden with avatar Pokémon on the loose, it's made the situation even worse."rPeople are getting attacked left and right, and the number of Trainers capable of killing one are pretty low."JHopefully we can train some more capable battlers in the near future."XThe computer glows faintly. A list of documents are organized into various folders."9The documents seem to be related to various avatars."UGym Leader Lambert reported an avatar he spotted in a grotto by Bluepoint Beach."HAccording to his follow-up, a Trainer managed to defeat the avatar."KRangers who investigated the scene confirmed that the avatar was gone."This place sucks."God, this place sucks."BI swear every fifteen seconds a new avatar is reported there."VThose kids living there are so lucky that, like, two capable Trainers live there."JI don't know what's with that spot. It has to be cursed or something."_Daily patrols are required. Nothing too bad has happened yet, but it could get much worse."tI swear I've been there like four times in three days. I don't even have the patience to write a proper report."5Well, peace or something. Dunno how to end this."7Multiple avatars have been reported in the sewers."While in other situations we might send some Rangers in, it's actually much easier to simply leave them to their business."vThere are only a few exits, which are staffed by sewer treatment personnel. Each of them are registered trainers."\The walls down there are hard to dig through, and Trainers rarely travel through there."^It's more efficient to leave the avatars down there until we have more Rangers available."cWitnesses observed multiple avatars destroy the bridge that connects Prizca to southern Makya."FThis has caused a large disturbance for intra- regional shipping."mThe situation isn't dire, but shipping to Németh and the LuxTech Campus has been limited to air travel."OThe avatar of Terrakion remains on the Prizca side of the bridge crossing."<Gigalith's Guts has been a hot spot of avatar activity."VParticularly strong avatars have been spotted both on the mountain and within it."[Rangers approaching the situation are advised to be in parties of no smaller than two."=Inexperienced Trainers are recommened to avoid the area."sTrainers looking to acquire the Patience and Perseverance Badges are recommended to travel via Grouz or Svait."WVelenz has been rendered unsafe for long term habitation due to the avatar crisis."�Operating Rangers have been able to keep the area at acceptable levels, enough for Rafael's Gym services to continue to function."9Non-Trainers are advised to avoid the area entirely."nPersonal Note: The situation is such a mess. We really need more staff on hand. Or funding. Or free food."GCan we get something other than camping rations over here? Please?"9Val has been complaining non-stop since we got here."- Connor"`Rangers patrolling Grouz have observed strange sightings of a potential four-legged avatar."~While previous patrols have confirmed the existence of avatar activity in the area, this particular sighting is rather unique."�Every avatar sighted in the area has been confirmed as Steel-type, and all known four-legged Steel-type Pokemon are too slow to match observed movement."`A local living in the area has reported multiple strange sightings in the surrounding area."�The proximity of his home to Gigalith's Guts makes his case plausible, but his reports don't seem to match the avatars known to be in the area."�Notably, he has also reported sighting two different Pokemon. The sighting locations and timings from other reports corroborate his story."^The destruction left at the sites of each sighting suggest an incredibly powerful avatar."bRangers looking to confirm these reports are advised to be in parties of no smaller than two."Closed Incidents"Known Incidents"Undefined Incidents"Log Off"Bluepoint Grotto"Németh Apartments"Sewers"Go Back"Eleig Bridge"Gigalith's Guts"Velenz"Grouz Sightings"County Park Sightings"^Now all of a sudden with avatar Pokemon on the loose, it's made the situation even worse."oThe situation isn't dire, but shipping to Novo Town and the LuxTech Campus has been limited to air travel.">Inexperienced Trainers are recommended to avoid the area."zOperating Rangers have been able to keep the area at acceptable levels, enough for Rafael's Gym services to continue."9Van has been complaining non-stop since we got here.[S"UPara combatir el crimen, tienes que mantener a ti y tus Pokémon en buena forma."VTanto física como mentalmente. Ahí fuera, tu cuerpo y mente están bajo ataque."ITener una grieta va a llevar a la otra a romperse aún más rápido."Toma esto."gÚsalo si te ayuda, pero lo más importante es que un cuerpo perfecto necesita una mente perfecta."qSi un día te cansas de combatir y quieres un cambio de ritmo, siempre estamos buscando por nuevas reclutas."pEstamos haciendo operaciones por toda la regió, así que podrás ver todo lo que Makya tiene para ofrecer."RAyudo a coordinar operaciones de rescate con algunos de los rangers de Makya."�Solíamos trabajar sólo alrededor de la Cueva Hielo, pero hemos sido financiados por LuxTech para empezar a hacer operaciones por toda la región."Ha sido duro.":Pokémon extraños han estado apareciendo de la nada."UUn montón de las cavernas de Makya han sido consideradas inseguras para viajar."_Nos manejamos, pero si la gente parara de ser tan descuidada, eso nos ayudaría demasiado."(Las montañas aquí son peligrosas."�Túneles de viento, caminos sin salida, y caminos circulares lo hacen un laberinto para hasta los montañeros con más experiencia."TY ahora de pronto con los Pokémon avatares sueltos, la situacion es aún peor."zLa gente está siendo atacada por izquierda y derecha, y el número de Entrenadores capaces de matar a uno son pocos."OEsperamos poder entrenar a más entrenadores capaces en el futuro cercano."cLa computadora brilla tenuemente. Una lista de documentos está organizada en varias carpetas."ALos documentos parecen estar relacionados a varios avatares."qEl Líder de Gimnasio Lambert reportó un avatar que fue detectado en una gruta cerca de la Playa Bluepoint."HDe acuerdo al seguimiento, un Entrenador logró derrotar al avatar."QLos Rangers que investigaron el lugar confimaron que el avatar ya no estaba."Este lugar apesta."Dios, este lugar apesta."FJuro que cada quince segundos un nuevo avatar es reportado allí."cLos niños viviendo allí tienen tanta suerte que, como, dos Entrenadores capaces viven allí."?No sé qué pasa con ese lugar. Debe estar maldito o algo."ePatrullas diarias son requeridas. Nada malo ha pasado todavía, pero podría ponerse mucho peor."�Juro que he estado ahí como cuatro veces en tres días. Ni siquiero tengo la paciencia para escribir un reporte en condiciones."3Bueno, paz o algo. No sé cómo terminar esto."BMúltiples avatares han sido reportados en las alcantarillas."{Mientras en otras situaciones enviaríamos unos Rangers, de hecho es mucho más fácil simplemente dejarlos a lo suyo."�Hay sólo un par de salidas, que están resguardadas por personal del tratamiento de las alcantarillas. Cada uno de ellos son entrenadores registrados."cEs difícil excavar atravesando por las paredes, y los entrenadores raramente viajan por ahí."cEs más eficiente dejar a los avatares ahí abajo hasta que tengamos más Rangers disponibles."hTestigos observaron múltiples avatares destruir el puente que conecta Prizca con Makya meridional."NEsto ha causado una gran perturbación para los envíos intra-regionales."|La situación no es urgente, pero los envíos desde Pueblo Novo hacia el Campus LuxTech han sido limitados a viajes aéreos."FEl avatar de Terrakion permanece en el lado de Prizca del puente."ELas Tripas de Gigalith ha sido el foco de actividad de avatares."cAvatares particularmente fuertes han sido reportados tanto en la montaña como dentro de esta."pA los Rangers acercándose a la situación se les recomiendo estar en equipos de por lo menos dos personas."GSe recomienda a Entrenadores con poca experiencia evitar el área."�A los entrenadores buscando conseguir las Medallas Paciencia y Perseverancia se les recomienda viajar a través de Grouz o Svait."eVelenz ha sido declarada insegura para habitar a largo plazo debido a la crisis de los avatares."�Los Rangers operativos han podido mantener el área a niveles aceptables, suficiente para que los servicios del Gimnasio de Rafael puedan seguir funcionando."CSe aconseja a los No-Entrenadores evitar el área enteramente."nNota Personal: La situación es un desastre. Necesitamos más personal a mano. O fondos. O comida gratis."U¿Podemos conseguir algo más que raciones de 