"]The storage PC in the Pokemon Center here is busted, so we set up an impromptu one here."You're free to use it."IWe rangers are trying to keep the avatar problem here under control."The results have been..."Less than optimal.Iu;␀Y[[�""An extreme force pushes back!"3A booklet emblazoned with the Team Chasm logo."...Your phone is ringing."2It’s... your mother. It’s Mavis. Pick up?"8Hey, \PN? I’ve been trying to call you for hours!"�Congratulations! You decimated Zain in the tournament, and my boots on the ground are telling me that you’ve done some extracurriculars."[Saved the region, I hear? Very impressive, \PN. You shattered my wildest expectations."�Now, I haven’t been able to get in contact with Zain, but to be honest, after that showing...? I’m not sure we have much to talk about right now."sIgnore him, though. He’s just moping because he couldn’t beat you. To be honest, I never thought he could."�Today’s about you. Aww, honey, you did so well! I can get a private flight scheduled to get you back home ASAP. I’ve got big plans for you."�You are my number one asset right now, and I want to show you the vacation you deserve. Business can wait – but there will be business."qWith your skills and my influence, I’ll secure you an exceedingly comfortable position within the company.".So, what date works for you to come home?"bTomorrow morning? Or do you want to sleep in? We’ll make it tomorrow evening, just in case."YYou – you what? Excuse me? Is there some kind of arrangement I don’t know about?"_Are you – are you eloping? Have you been offered a job there? You do understand what –"FOh, good. I’ll start making plans for our vacation immediately."#You’ve worked so hard and..."AMavis continues on for a few minutes before she lets you go."JShe says she loves you, and goodbye, and she’ll see you again soon."MYou’ll tell her that a certain someone said hi when you meet her next.":You’ll be her second-in-command and second-to-last."0...You thought it’d make you feel warmer."9You’ve never not picked up for your mother before."&It’s Mavis. You have to answer."...No, you don’t."2You? I... I remember... outside of Novo Town.">You aren’t – I mean, you are – it doesn’t matter."OYou’re here. I’m here. I have more Pokémon to train. A duel? Doubles.":W-well, I could ask you the same thing. Can we start?"?Then go! Don’t bother me and then not even – whatever."5But you’re not getting past me without a duel."ASo? I’m not moving until I get a double battle out of you."-Good. OK. No more talking. Just... this."9That was -- you’re... yeah, you are, aren’t you?"fIf you’re looking deeper in the caves, then I -- I mean, if you don’t mind, may I come along?"�I have healing items for the both of us. It’s dangerous and we -- I’d like to talk. And that’s... that’s not very common for me."9So? I’m not moving until I get a fight out of you.",I need to... oh, just fight me already!":That was – you’re... yeah, you are, aren’t you?"gIf you’re looking deeper in the caves, then I – I mean, if you don’t mind, may I come along?";Ah, you’re back. I, uh, don’t have much to do yet.".And we still haven’t finished our talk."2Some loose paper displaying the LuxTech logo." So you lead with \pfp, hmm?".Tell me – would you tell me about them?"-Good, good. You seem to be good friends."hMy Togekiss, Artemisia, has been mine since I was – oh, sorry. I shouldn’t... let’s continue.".Oh, is that so? Well, maybe it’ll grow."bMy Togekiss, Artemisia, used to be a liability, but she became my most trusted – excuse me.":I’m – why am I – whatever. Let’s keep moving."%I’m glad you found them, then."bThe only reason I have Artemisia, my Togekiss, is a story about a Togekiss from my childhood."MI’ve loved – sorry. I’m getting carried away – let’s continue."*Hah, well, I know what that’s like."QI rarely get to use my true team – my, uh, friends give me teams to train."mMy Togekiss, Artemisia, gets used more for flying than – oh, I’m – excuse me. Let’s keep moving."LLeaving through -- oh. You -- you’re looking for something down here."2Come back and, uh, I’ll still be... around.":Were you down here for this – whatever all this is?"'That Linoone dragged it down here."8Even if you weren’t… it’s valuable. Trust me."3Barter and blackmail are Makya’s currencies."SAnd this <imp>Chasm keycard</imp> – I haven’t – it’s been a long time."<Take it. I don’t need it, and Helena won’t miss it.";It’ll get you into some <imp>dangerous places</imp>."I used to – oh."XOh. Oh, I just – I – I’m sorry. I shouldn’t be imposing upon you like this."KI’ve been stalking you – I just – my name’s <imp>Yezera</imp>."Yours?"0Well, \PN, you... you’re easy to talk to."VAlmost like a Pokémon, and I just – I’ve never found someone… I’m sorry.";I just keep talking and – I should go. I need to go."eOh – I mean, yes, that’s... I’m sorry. I’m a stranger, I shouldn’t’ve – I’ll go."But thank you."�I – I haven’t talked to someone in... a little while, and you’re… I don’t know why but you’re easy to – I’m sorry."I should go."RAnother avatar... so strange. They aren’t spirits – not like Ghost-types."cI’ve never found an avatar of a man-made Pokémon, but there are avatars of fossil Pokémon."Almost as if... hmm." What do you think they are?"AOh – uh, I’m sorry, I’m not used to getting responses."I mostly talk to Pokémon."GPlease excuse my rambling, I – but you’re right. Nobody knows."COh – I suppose – sorry, I’m used to talking to Pokémon."AI’m not used to my rambling being – I mean, I’m sorry."/You said illusions? And yet they... hmm..."VOh – you – I’m sorry, excuse my ramblings. I usually talk to, um, Pokémon."/And they don’t – I mean – ignore me.">But you have a good hypothesis, I think. Except... hmm..."mOh – I didn’t – sorry. Excuse me, I forgot that you – I mean, I’m used to talking to Pokémon."EI’m – I’m not used to… whatever. Forget I said anything."Pick up."Don't pick up."I'm not coming home."That sounds nice."What are you doing here?"Not now."OK."It's reliable."It's lackluster."It's my favorite."I'm just training it."Tell her."Don't tell her."I don't know."Illusions."Myths made real."I don't care."^\wm\ss\l[3]By entering this door, you will cause events that <imp>cannot be undone</imp>."f\wm\ss\l[3]If there are still more stories to live, this is your <imp>last chance</imp> to do so."Stay out."Enter."/...Ain’t really feelin’ it today, \PN."iY’know, I’m a fan of yours, gotta admit. Like your style. Like how you move. Like how you fight."�Remind me of Yez, more than a li’l. But... I just ain’t feelin’ up to small talk. Today’s a day for big happenings, y’see?"aSure hope so. It ain’t exactly subtle. So, now, let’s figure this out 'tween you and me."YWhich of us is better, who’s gonna be the one going down there, the whole shebang."EYou even gotta ask ‘bout that? Y’know how this goes. Always."|Ain’t no other way for us folks. We got somethin’ to figure out: which one of us is gonna have to give Yez a talking-to."\Oh, don’tcha go callin’ it a crush. Just got a lot of traits I’m half-partial to."MAin’t 'bout to change what we gotta do. One of us gotta go down there."EI’m her friend. You’re her... well, you’re a lotta things."YI figure you got a better chance of beating her than I do, but I gotta double-check."uAw, who am I kiddin’? I’m nervous, kid. I ain’t got the guts to face her and tell her what needs sayin’.",So c’mon. Gimme an excuse to give up."@Figured if there was one thing ya could do, it’d be this."Hah! Knew I liked you.":Nah. Never could say no to her, not when it mattered."bYou let me know when you’re 'bout ready, and we’ll do this. Ain’t no two ways about it."YTake your time and make it good. I wanna be facin’ the whole nine yards, y’hear?";Ah, good. Prove me right. Show me I ain’t nothin’."{But, uh, I ain’t ‘bout to go down easy. \PN, meet the team I’ve been honing since the good ol’ days. Meet Drag-Mag."...'Bout figures."nWell, I ain’t gonna sugarcoat it: it’s your job now. Always was, lookin’ at it a certain kinda way."_Go down there. Talk some sense into her. Y’know how. Ain’t much else to say, is there?"NYou know whatcha gotta do. Don’t need me holdin’ your hand. Good kid."^Oh, don’tcha go thankin’ me yet. I ain’t done nothin’ for ya. Nothin’ material."I was plannin’ to."�I ain’t ‘bout to go down there myself with ya – it’s a private affair. Can’t ruin my reputation by barging on in and making a muck of things."`Hah. Don’t embarrass me. Maybe after all’s said and done, we can grab a drink together."@You, me, Yez... or just you and me, if that’s your drift."QJust don’tcha go being one of those folks asking me to step on ‘em. Hah!"BYou’re gonna need a li’l help to get to tomorrow, though."�Take my Heatran. I don’t see myself fightin’ too many wars in my near future, and for anythin’ less my regulars will do well enough."7You, though? You oughta take anything you can get."ATake good care of that damn thing, y’hear? We go way back."rAnd, besides, it’s a damn juggernaut that can wreak more carnage than a babyface like you can even imagine."wHah! I ain’t never been able to tell if you’re brave or stupid. In my experience, they ain’t much different."ZAs you say, though. Ain’t gonna complain 'bout keepin’ an extra ace up my sleeve."�Well, I s’pose we oughta keep it brief, all things considered. You gotta go hunt that girl down, and I gotta go prep for either which way it ends."I’ll be seein’ her soon, one way or another. Probably won’t be too keen on seein’ me, but that’s friends for ya."SHey, \PN, I figure this comes as an awful surprise to you, but I got a secret."�Up until now, I’ve been workin’ with Yez, clandestine-like. Masked, causin’ havoc, fightin’ you. I ain’t proud of it, but it ain’t far from my usual."xI’m a black ops gal born and raised, though I’m a mite more on the side of cut-and-burn than cloak-and- dagger."rI ain’t 'bout to apologize. But, uh, Yez’d have me stoppin’ you, and I ain’t 'bout to play that game."IShe got other lackeys, good on her, but I ain't gonna be one of 'em."1Go ruin her day, kid. I’ll see you around."fHey, next time I see ya, drinks are on me. Call it my way of making up to you. Heh. So long, kid."X\PN, go ruin her day. I wish I was good enough to do it myself, but I just ain’t."RYou understand her well enough. She’ll listen to you, one way or the other."~And, uh, sorry. For makin’ this all ‘bout her. If things were any different, I’d love to chat ‘bout other things."<Maybe some day, yeah? I’ll see you around, I promise."nYou come back and there’s still bars left in the world, drinks are on me, y’hear? See ya around, kid."I'm not prepared yet."I am ready."I know."So now what?"You like me?"
