 they might go, but I am not worried. They seem content."2I have seen my own life sink below the waves."!I want to save what is left."VI am simply enjoy the last of my home. This soothing breeze will the be the last."SPlease, you have lived on this island with us for generations for generations!"'What could we possibly offer now?!"JThere is not much time left for my home. I will enjoy it while I can."`I thank you for giving me an excellent parting memory. Now, it's time to go to my new home."MI am sad I cannot spend my twilight years here. That is life, I suppose."It is time for a picnic."/You would not know our devotion, outsider."6It is over. There is nothing left to do but wait."-Oh, hi! I was expecting ya from Vincent."5Uhhhhhh... Welcome! To our uhhh... humble abode?"�We used to get more guests a looooong time ago, but we don't get them much now. I guess a sinking island isn't the best place for investors..."POh well! Can't save 'em all... just uhh... enjoy it while it lasts? Haha..."mAnyways! We have a healing center! I'm qualified a nurse, actually! Just don't have the typical uniform."wWe certainly like to battle here on this island! Just like uhhh... literally every other person... So that's cool!"Anyways I'll be in that building behind me if you need me! Ummm, enjoy your stay and uhhh... talk with some of the locals!"#Leave us to our ways, Trainer."HYou had to meddle. We have lost our traditions due to you, Trainer."^Ah, a visitor. It is rare to see one nowadays. I can hardly remember the last one's face."XIt's a shame. Memory is the only thing we have, and the only tool we can work with."3Tell me Trainer, what is your greatest memory?"`A mighty accomplishment indeed. I wonder, will it be your favorite when you lose the title?"vYou possess a full heart, Trainer. I wonder, will it be your favorite after you have seen them for the last time?"iA feat of courage, and a show of strength! I wonder, will it be your favorite when your anger cools?"bIt is wise to look forward. I wonder, will it be your favorite when you only have the future?"RThis island, our home, will soon be nothing but a memory. What an awful fate."IThere is nothing that can be done other than making one last memory."]A final hurrah before the shore closes in. A battle to shatter this island's very roots."'Are you ready, Trainer, to battle?"GThere are memories to be made, Trainer. Do not leave me apathetic."(A disappointment, to say the least."SIf there is one think I know though, it is that minds can change. Change mine."<Very well, I shall be here, looking for another memory."0I suppose that's that then. A final memory."VIt was not unpleasent, Trainer. It was the best we could do in such a short time."�If you would like, this is our farewell. Soon, we will fade into each other's memory. Some time after, we will fade even further than that."nBut perhaps, there is something more. I must gather myself inside my little cove. You are free to follow."'I cannot let all this just happen!"*There is nothing left for us to do..."fI ache Trainer! There is hole in one's self when they lose their home, it is a heart torn in two!"kThe past has always been outside of our reach. And yet, when you cannot see it, it feels even further."�And yet, I do not feel despair. I feel bittersweet. When I think of home, it is impossible to not feel a little bit of warmth inside."gHave you felt that conflict before, Trainer? A feeling of warmth and joy that lives within sorrow?"I know your pain, Trainer."pThe world is never the same after someone leaves, but we are always glad that we got to live in that world."We think of the time spent with them, doing nothing. We regret it. Yet, that time is where they became who they are to us.".One day, maybe, we can forgive ourselves."/They never look at us the same afterwards."You realize you cannot imagine them without thinking about how their expression changed when they learned of your failure."aSometimes, it is a necessary mistake to make. There is no growth if we let ourselves simmer."4Then you are blessed now and cursed to feel it."]But that is life, young one. You must realize that, as we love to say, it is what it is."<I am filled with sorrow. It is the price I pay for joy."SBut I am not helpless. I choose to pay again and again. Each time it worth it."ONow, Trainer, will you show me a little bit of the joy you feel in battle?"hThere is no joy in battle without the bitterness of frustration. Let us pay your dues to our wiles."Ahah! Take that!"bA-hem, I mean, frustration is a natural part of growth. Grow, and approach me again, Trainer."6Afriad? Or cautious? Ah, well, it doesn't matter."-I will be here. We all smile eventually."@Perhaps you have caught a glimpse of that feeling, Trainer."rIt matters not, you will feel it soon enough. It will feel wonderful and awful and all of those great things."?I will collect my feelings before I leave. I'll be inside."9If you would like to follow, you are more than free."'A guest! What a pleasant surprise!"KHave you come to challenge me? I have a bit of time to test my mettle."MAh, but before we get too far ahead of myself, I must sate my curiosity."[You seem no stranger to struggle, but tell me, have you ever been broken by challenge?"RUtterly shattered. Reduced. Something you viewed as damningly insurmountable?"jHmm, bold. It is one thing to break yourself for another. It is another for them to mock your pieces."RIt can be a moment that defines your world, and you are not in control of it."{And you certainly you gained something in the end! Of course, you know as well as any that the real danger lies afterwards."VIt is one thing to climb a mountain once. It is another to climb a hill each day."8If honesty were a virtue, you'd qualify as a saint." Not that it's a good thing."�Then there is something you must do, now! There is a wide open world out there, but you must be torn down for a new life to grow!"hBut I digress. The force of will takes man and mon far, but it cannot always overcome cold reality."?This island will be gone. There are some that refute that."pSometimes, there is value in fighting the inevitable. Sometimes. I am never sure about it until it is over."QThere are those who try to preserve this place, as foolish as that might be."TI wonder how it will end up for them. It is a good trial, and a proper funeral."mBut that is them. I should focus on myself. I am ready for challenge. Are you ready for battle, Trainer?"Excellent!"ANow is the time! Let us break and reform from our struggles!"%And you lay before me in pieces."bThere's only one direction to go from here. Regain youself, and try again. You can do better.">Very well, but do not leave me waiting. I abhor idleness."OI am looking for one last trail myself. Are you ready for battle, Trainer?"4Wonderful! It was about time for me to shatter!"lI revel in that sting you get when you know you've been outmatched! It is undeniable, how jealous I am!">But such a feeling is fleeting, for better and for worse."TIt's time for me to get ready for the next hill. I'll be inside if you need me.";These Guardians have been here since before all of us."9If there is a way forward, they will bring us there."/You have snuffed out any hope that we had."1I'm not sure that it was a good or bad deed."(We seek its power to heal our home.""Please, you must have a plan!"0Centuries of guidance cannot end like this!"VSo many here wish to give up our homeland. To what! Simple time and happenstance?"UI will depart, but I will be bitter. The spirit of our island will sink with it."LI am surrounded by fools! The sages are right! We must adapt or perish!"Leave me be, outsider."LMy Rampardos and I have a unique camaraderie. We suffer from hair loss."4I need to get a sick crown like my Rampardos..."5I must treat the little hair I have left kindly."#Mmm. Maybe I should buy a hat."eHon hon! This island has exceptional beauty! It is a shame I will be the last visitor to see it."TOh, are you also foreign to here? Well, that ruins the title of "last visitor"."1Ah, the locals here are so good at battling."/I think I'll enjoy a fine Kalosian wine..."ZLook towards the future, Trainer. You might miss how much of a mess the past becomes."2Come, my Pokemon. Let us take a final stroll."0It's a shame how the past has been tainted."IWe are old minded here. But our ways are nothing in front of nature."aWe like to forget that we are still a part of nature, no matter how high we build ourselves."Winning the Championship."Helping a friend."!Telling someone to buzz off."Letting go of my past."	Yes."Not right now."Yes, when I lost someone." Yes, when I failed someone."Yes, when I upset someone."No, I haven't felt that."Yes, to help someone."Yes, to gain something."Yes, to avoid my fears."No, I haven't."YI am simply enjoying the last of my home. This soothing breeze will the be the last."4Please, you have lived with us for generations!"CYou had to meddle. We have lost our traditions because of you!"I cannot let this happen!"You must have a plan![�"KEste laberinto es parte de las ruinas de una civilización ya perdida."`No hay duda de que hay algo de valor en él, pero no recomendaría entrar sin ningún plan."rLos Entrenadores que vienen aquí son bastante fuertes, por no mencionar los avatares que están en el área."�Si quieres entrar, pasa. La mayoría de Entrenadores que están más lejos de la mitad de su desafíos de los Gimnasios podrán arreglarsela."B¡Un pilar de piedra se ha levantado para bloquear tu salida!"-Los otros pilares pueden haber cambiado."/Hombre, realmente no debería estar aquí."(Supongo que nadie vendrá a ayudar."5Tendré que encontrar mi propia salida de aquí."?Podrías conseguir, ya sabes, ¿Algún adulto para ayudar?"BSupongo que ambos estamos, como, impresionantemente perdidos."$La energía en este lugar es…"¡Tentadora!")¡Increíble! Tu energía es fuerte."%Valió la pena hacer este viaje."CDeseo meditar aquí más tiempo. Hasta la proxima, Entrenador."JSi escuchas con atención, puedes escuchar los susurros de la jungla."#Es diferente en otros lugares."$Aquí, es un tono de un Pastor.")La puerta está fuermente bloqueada."CLos sabios desean invertir la muerte de la isla. Son ingenuos."ILa isla no puede ser salvada, ya la he visto junto a los fallecidos."?Quizás un foraster como tú tiene una perspectiva única."@Esta isla es antigua. Los espíritus aquí están cansados."LMe pregunto a dónde podrán ir, pero no me preouca. Parecen contentos."4He visto mi propia vida hundirse bajo las olas."#Quiero salvar lo que me queda."aEstoy simplemente disfrutando lo último de mi hogar. Esta relajante brisa será la última."`¡Por favor, tú que has vivido en esta isla con nosotros por generaciones de generaciones!"-¡¿Qué más podríamos ofrecer ahora?!"HNo le queda mucho tiempo a mi hogar. Lo disfrutaré mientras pueda."fTe agradezco por darme una excelente memoria de despedida. Ahora, es hora de ir a mi nuevo hogar."UMe entristece no poder pasar mis últimos años aquí. Así es la vida, supongo."Es hora de un picnic."2No conocerías nuestra devoción, extranjero."<Se acabó. No hay nada más que hacer más que esperar."2¡Oh, hola! Vincent me contó que llegarías."A¡Ehhhhhh... Bienvenido! A nuestra ehhh... ¿Humilde morada?"�Solíamos tener más turistas hace muuuuuucho tiempo, pero ya no vienen mucho ahora. Supongo que una isla hundiéndose no es el mejor lugar para los inversores…"_¡Oh bueno! No puedes salvarlo todo… sólo ehh… ¿Disfrútalo mientras puedas? Jaja…"{¡Como sea! ¡Tenemos un centro de curación! ¡Soy una enfermera calificada, de hecho! Sólo no tengo el uniforme típico."�¡Ciertamente nos gusta combatir en esta isla! Sólo ehhh… pregúntale a literalmente cualquier otra persona… ¡Así que bien!"¡Como sea, estaré en esa casa detrás mío si me necesitas! Emmm, disfruta tu estadía y ehhh… ¡Habla con algunos locales!"'Déjanos a lo nuestro, Entrenador."[Tenías que entrometerte. Hemos perdido nuestras tradiciones por tu culpa, Entrenador."aAh, un visitante. Es raro ver uno en estos días. Apenas puedo recordar la cara del último."oEs una lástima. La memoria es lo único que tenemos, y la única herramienta con la que podemos trabajar.";Dime Entrenador, ¿Cuál es tu recuerdo más preciado?"TPor supuesto, un gran logro. Me pregunto, ¿Lo será cuando pierdas el título?"jPosees un corazón puro, Entrenador. Me pregunto, ¿Lo será luego de haberlos visto por última vez?"i¡Una proeza de valor, y una muestra de fuerza! Me pregunto, ¿Lo será cuando tu enojo desaparezca?"YEs sabio mirar hacia delante. Me pregunto, ¿Lo será cuando sólo tengas el futuro?"WEsta isla, nuestro hogar, no será nada más que un recuerdo. Un destino horrible."CNo hay nada más que hacer más que crear un último recuerdo."mUn último hurra antes de que la costa desaparezca. Un combate para destruir los cimientos de esta isla."/¿Estás listo, Entrenador, para combatir?"?Hay memorias que formar, Entrenador. No me dejes apático."'Decepcionante, por decir lo menos."`Pero si hay una cosa que sé, es que las mentalidades pueden ser cambiadas. Cambia la mía."4Muy bien, estaré aquí, buscando otra memoria."<Supongo que así termina entonces. Un último recuerdo."YNo fue decepcionante, Entrenador. Fue lo mejor que pudimos hacer en tan poco tiempo."�Si te parece, esto es nuestro adiós. Pronto, nos desvaneceremos en la memoria del otro. Un tiempo después de eso, nos desvaneceremos incluso más allá."gPero quizás, hay algo más. Debo meditar dentro de mi pequeña bovedilla. Eres libre de seguirme."+¡No puedo dejer que todo esto ocurra!"*No hay nada más que podamos hacer…"p¡Me duele Entrenador! ¡Hay un agujero en cada uno cuando pierden su hogar, es un corazón partido en dos!"~El pasado siempre ha estado fuera de nuestro alcance. Y aún así, cuando no puedes verlo, se siente incluso más lejano."�Y aún así, no me siento desesperado. Es agridulce. Cuando pienso en mi hogar, es imposible no sentir algo de calor dentro de mi."{¿Has sentido ese conflicto antes, Entrenador? ¿Un sentido de calor y felicidad que vive alrededor de la melancolía?""Conozco tu dolor, Entrenador."xEl mundo nunca es el mismo luego de que alguien se va, pero siempre estamos contentos de haber vivido en ese mundo."�Pensamos en el tiempo que pasamos con ellos, sin hacer nada. Lo lamentamos. Y aún así, ese tiempo es cuando se convierten en lo que fueron para nosotros.",Un día, quizás, podremos perdonarnos."3Luego nunca nos ven a nosotros del mismo modo."tTe das cuenta de que no puedes imaginártelos sin pensar en cómo su expresión cuando aprendieron de tu error."eA veces, es un error necesario que hacer. No hay desarrollo si dejamos que la rabia nos consuma."=Entonces estás bendecido ahora y maldito para sentirlo."_Pero así es la vida, jóven. Debes darte cuenta de eso, como amamos decir, es lo que hay,"HEstoy lleno de melancolía. Es el precio que pago por la felicidad."YPero no estoy indefenso. Deseo pagarlo de nuevo y de nuevo. Y cada vez vale la pena."VAhora, Entrenador. ¿Me mostrarás un poco de la alegría que sientes en combate?"tNo hay alegría en combate sin la amargura de la frustración. Déjanos pagar nuestra parte con nuestro tiempo."¡Jaja! ¡Toma eso!"zEjem, quiero decir, la frustración es la parte natural del desarrollo. Crece, y vuelve conmigo otra vez, Entrenador."7¿Con miedo? ¿O cauteloso? Oh, bueno, no importa."5Estaré aquí. Todos sonreíremos eventualmente."JQuizás has alcanzado a ver una parte de ese sentimiento, Entrenador."~No importa, ya que la sentirás lo suficientemente pronto. Se sentirá maravilloso y horrible y todas esas grandes cosas."DVoy a pensar en mis sentimientos antes de irme. Estaré dentro."3Si quieres seguirme, eres más que bienvenido."/¡Un visitante! ¡Vaya agradable sorpresa!"Q¿Has venido a desafiarme? Tengo un poco de tiempo para demostrar mi coraje."?Ah, pero antes de ir muy lejos, debo saciar mi curiosidad."lPareces estar familiarizado con las dificultades, pero dime, ¿Alguna vez has sido roto por un desafio?"`Absolutamente destruído. Reducido. ¿Algo que has visto como irremisiblemente insuperable?"kHmm, atrevido. Una cosa es romperte a ti mismo por otro. Es otra cosa distinta burlarse de tus piezas."XPuede ser un momento que definte tu mundo, y que tú no tienes control al respecto."{¡Y ciertamente has ganado algo al final! Por supuesto, conoces bien como todos que el verdadero peligro yace luego de eso."YEs una cosa escalar una montaña una vez. Otra cosa es escalar una colina cada día."HSi la honestidad fuera una virtud, tú calificarías como un santo."(No es como si eso fuera algo bueno."�¡Entonces hay algo que debes hacer, ahora! ¡Hay todo un vasto mundo ahí fuera, pero tú debes ser demolido para que una nueva vida crezca!"Cambiando de tema. La fuerza de voluntad lleva al hombre y al mon lejos, pero no siempre puede superar a la dura realidad."9La isla dejará de ser. Hay algunos que refutan eso."oA veces, hay valor en combatir lo inevitable. A veces. Nunca estoy seguro al respecto hasta que se acabó."YEstán aquellos que intentan preservar el lugar, con lo ingenuo que eso puede sonar."VMe pregunto cómo terminará para ellos. Es una buena prueba, y un funeral digno."�Pero eso son ellos. Debería concentrarme en mí mismo. Estoy listo para un desafío. ¿Estás listo para un combate, Entrenador?"¡Excelente!"O¡Ahora es la hora! ¡Déjanos rompernos y reformarnos de nuestras luchas!"&Y tú recaes ante mí en pedazos."qSólo hay una dirección a la que puedas ir ahora. Recupéerta, e inténtalo de nuevo. Puedes hacerlo mejor."BMuy bien, pero no me dejes esperando. Aborrezco la ociosidad."VY estoy buscando por un último rastro. ¿Estás listo para combatir, Entrenador?"4¡Maravilloso! ¡Era hora para que me rompiera!"u¡Me regocijo en la punzada que obtienes cuando sabes que has sido superado! ¡Es innegable lo celoso que estoy!"<Pero tal sentimiento es efímero, para bien o para mal."VEs la hora de que vaya a por mi siguiente colina. Estaré dentro si me necesitas."GEstos Guardiantes han estado aquí desde antes que todos nosotros.">Si hay un camino hacia delante, ellos nos traerán allí."3Has extinguido toda esperanza que nos quedaba."DNo estoy seguro de que esto haya sido una buena o mala acción."0Buscamos su poder para sanar nuestro hogar."&¡Por favor, debes tener un plan!"6¡Centenarios de guianza no pueden terminar así!"^Tantos aquí desean renunciar a nuestra tierra natal. ¡A qué! ¿Al tiempo y casualidad?"TPartiré, pero con amargura. El espíritu de nuestra isla se hundirá con ella."]¡Estoy rodeado de idiotas! ¡Los sabios tienen la razón! ¡Debemos adaptarnos o morir!"Déjame estar, forastero."VMi Rampardos y yo sufrimos una camaradería única. Sufrimos de pérdida capilar."<Debo conseguir una tremenda corona como mi Rampardos…"7Debo tratar al poco pelo que me queda con cariño."/Mmm. Quizás debería comprar un sombrero."s¡Jo jo! ¡Esta isla tiene una maravilla excepcional! Es una lástima que seré el último visitante en verla."d¿Oh, también eres extrañero aquí? Bueno, eso arruina el título de “último visitante”."6Ah, los locales aquí son tan buenos en combatir."2Creo que disfrutaré un fino vino de Kalos…"eMira hacia el futuro, entrenador. Podrías perderte todo el desastre que se convierte el pasado."8Ven, mis Pokémon. Déjanos tomar un último paseo."4Es una lástima cómo el pasado se ha manchado."hSomos viejos de mente aquí. Pero nuestros caminos no son nada más que el frente de la naturaleza."dSolemos olvidar que todavía somos parte de la naturaleza, no importa lo alto que nos pongamos."Ganar el Campeonato."Ayudar a un amigo."#Decirle a alguien que se vaya."Dejar atrás a mi pasado."	Sí."No ahora mismo.""Sí, cuando perdí a alguien."%Sí, cuando le fallé a alguien."$Sí, cuando molesté a alguien."No, no he sentido eso." Sí, para ayudar a alguien."Sí, para ganar algo."!Sí, para evitar mis miedos."No, no lo he hecho."hSimplemente estoy disfrutando los últimos momentos de mi hogar. Esta suave brisa será la última.";Por favor, ¡has vivido con nosotros por generaciones!"JTuviste que entrometer. ¡Perdimos nuestras tradiciones por tu culpa!"&¡No puedo dejar que esto ocurra!"¡Debes tener un plan!;[�"@This maze is part of the ruins of a long-lost civilization."hNo doubt that's there's something of value in it, but I wouldn't recommend going in without a plan."dThe Trainers that come here are pretty strong, not to mention the avatars that are in the area."wIf you want to go in, be my guest. Most Trainers more than halfway through their Gym challenge can hold their own."1A stone piller has risen to block your exit!"2The other pillers might have changed as well."(Man, I really shouldn't be in here.",I guess no one's really coming to help."'Gotta find my own way out of here."4Can you get like, a more adult-y adult to help?"1I guess we're both, like, impressively lost."#The energy in this place is..."Tantalizing!"$Amazing! Your energy is strong."&It was worth it to make the trip."<I wish to meditate here more. Until next time, Trainer."?If you listen closely, you can hear the jungle's whispers."%It is different in other places." Here, it is a Shepard tone."!The door is securely locked."DThe sages wish to reverse the island's death. They are foolish."GThe island cannot be saved, I have already seen it among the dead.";Perhaps an outsider like you has a unique perspective."6This island is old. There spirits here are tired."KI wonder where they might go, but I am not worried. They seem content."2I have seen my own life sink below the waves."!I want to save what is left."VI am simply enjoy the last of my home. This soothing breeze will the be the last."SPlease, you have lived on this island with us for generations for generations!"'What could we possibly offer now?!"JThere is not much time left for my home. I will enjoy it while I can."`I thank you for giving me an excellent parting memory. Now, it's time to go to my new home."MI am sad I cannot spend my twilight years here. That is life, I suppose."It is time for a picnic."/You would not know our devotion, outsider."6It is over. There is nothing left to do but wait."-Oh, hi! I was expecting ya from Vincent."5Uhhhhhh... Welcome! To our uhhh... humble abode?"�We used to get more guests a looooong time ago, but we don't get them much now. I guess a sinking island isn't the best place for investors..."POh well! Can't save 'em all... just uhh... enjoy it while it lasts? Haha..."mAnyways! We have a healing center! I'm qualified a nurse, actually! Just don't have the typical uniform."wWe certainly like to battle here on this island! Just like uhhh... literally every other person... So that's cool!"Anyways I'll be in that building behind me if you need me! Ummm, enjoy your stay and uhhh... talk with some of the locals!"#Leave us to our ways, Trainer."HYou had to meddle. We have lost our traditions due to you, Trainer."^Ah, a visitor. It is rare to see one nowadays. I can hardly remember the last one's face."XIt's a shame. Memory is the only thing we have, and the only tool we can work with."3Tell me Trainer, what is your greatest memory?"`A mighty accomplishment indeed. I wonder, will it be your favorite when you lose the title?"vYou possess a full heart, Trainer. I wonder, will it be your favorite after you have seen them for the last time?"iA feat of courage, and a show of strength! I wonder, will it be your favorite when your anger cools?"bIt is wise to look forward. I wonder, will it be your favorite when you only have the future?"RThis island, our home, will soon be nothing but a memory. What an awful fate."IThere is nothing that can be done other than making one last memory."]A final hurrah before the shore closes in. A battle to shatter this island's very roots."'Are you ready, Trainer, to battle?"GThere are memories to be made, Trainer. Do not leave me apathetic."(A disappointment, to say the least."SIf there is one think I know though, it is that minds can change. Change mine."<Very well, I shall be here, looking for another memory."0I suppose that's that then. A final memory."VIt was not unpleasent, Trainer. It was the best we could do in such a short time."�If you would like, this is our farewell. Soon, we will fade into each other's memory. Some time after, we will fade even further than that."nBut perhaps, there is something more. I must gather myself inside my little cove. You are free to follow."'I cannot let all this just happen!"*There is nothing left for us to do..."fI ache Trainer! There is hole in one's self when they lose their home, it is a heart torn in two!"kThe past has always been outside of our reach. And yet, when you cannot see it, it feels even further."�And yet, I do not feel despair. I feel bittersweet. When I think of home, it is impossible to not feel a little bit of warmth inside."gHave you felt that conflict before, Trainer? A feeling of warmth and joy that lives within sorrow?"I know your pain, Trainer."pThe world is never the same after someone leaves, but we are always glad that we got to live in that world."We think of the time spent with them, doing nothing. We regret it. Yet, that time is where they became who they are to us.".One day, maybe, we can forgive ourselves."/They never look at us the same afterwards."You realize you cannot imagine them without thinking about how their expression changed when they learned of your failure."aSometimes, it is a necessary mistake to make. There is no growth if we let ourselves simmer."4Then you are blessed now and cursed to feel it."]But that is life, young one. You must realize that, as we love to say, it is what it is."<I am filled with sorrow. It is the price I pay for joy."SBut I am not helpless. I choose to pay again and again. Each time it worth it."ONow, Trainer, will you show me a little bit of the joy you feel in battle?"hThere is no joy in battle without the bitterness of frustration. Let us pay your dues to our wiles."Ahah! Take that!"bA-hem, I mean, frustration is a natural part of growth. Grow, and approach me again, Trainer."6Afriad? Or cautious? Ah, well, it doesn't matter."-I will be here. We all smile eventually."@Perhaps you have caught a glimpse of that feeling, Trainer."rIt matters not, you will feel it soon enough. It will feel wonderful and awful and all of those great things."?I will collect my feelings before I leave. I'll be inside."9If you would like to follow, you are more than free."'A guest! What a pleasant surprise!"KHave you come to challenge me? I have a bit of time to test my mettle."MAh, but before we get too far ahead of myself, I must sate my curiosity."[You seem no stranger to struggle, but tell me, have you ever been broken by challenge?"RUtterly shattered. Reduced. Something you viewed as damningly insurmountable?"jHmm, bold. It is one thing to break yourself for another. It is another for them to mock your pieces."RIt can be a moment that defines your world, and you are not in control of it."{And you certainly you gained something in the end! Of course, you know as well as any that the real danger lies afterwards."VIt is one thing to climb a mountain once. It is another to climb a hill each day."8If honesty were a virtue, you'd qualify as a saint." Not that it's a good thing."�Then there is something you must do, now! There is a wide open world out there, but you must be torn down for a new life to grow!"hBut I digress. The force of will takes man and mon far, but it cannot always overcome cold reality."?This island will be gone. There are some that refute that."pSometimes, there is value in fighting the inevitable. Sometimes. I am never sure about it until it is over."QThere are those who try to preserve this place, as foolish as that might be."TI wonder how it will end up for them. It is a good trial, and a proper funeral."mBut that is them. I should focus on myself. I am ready for challenge. Are you ready for battle, Trainer?"Excellent!"ANow is the time! Let us break and reform from our struggles!"%And you lay before me in pieces."bThere's only one direction to go from here. Regain youself, and try again. You can do better.">Very well, but do not leave me waiting. I abhor idleness."OI am looking for one last trail myself. Are you ready for battle, Trainer?"4Wonderful! It was about time for me to shatter!"lI revel in that sting you get when you know you've been outmatched! It is undeniable, how jealous I am!">But such a feeling is fleeting, for better and for worse."TIt's time for me to get ready for the next hill. I'll be inside if you need me.";These Guardians have been here since before all of us."9If there is a way forward, they will bring us there."/You have snuffed out any hope that we had."1I'm not sure that it was a good or bad deed."(We seek its power to heal our home.""Please, you must have a plan!"0Centuries of guidance cannot end like this!"VSo many here wish to give up our homeland. To what! Simple time and happenstance?"UI will depart, but I will be bitter. The spirit of our island will sink with it."LI am surrounded by fools! The sages are right! We must adapt or perish!"Leave me be, outsider."LMy Rampardos and I have a unique camaraderie. We suffer from hair loss."4I need to get a sick crown like my Rampardos..."5I must treat the little hair I have left kindly."#Mmm. Maybe I should buy a hat."eHon hon! This island has exceptional beauty! It is a shame I will be the last visitor to see it."TOh, are you also foreign to here? Well, that ruins the title of "last visitor"."1Ah, the locals here are so good at battling."/I think I'll enjoy a fine Kalosian wine..."ZLook towards the future, Trainer. You might miss how much of a mess the past becomes."2Come, my Pokemon. Let us take a final stroll."0It's a shame how the past has been tainted."IWe are old minded here. But our ways are nothing in front of nature."aWe like to forget that we are still a part of nature, no matter how high we build ourselves."Winning the Championship."Helping a friend."!Telling someone to buzz off."Letting go of my past."	Yes."Not right now."Yes, when I lost someone." Yes, when I failed someone."Yes, when I upset someone."No, I haven't felt that."Yes, to help someone."Yes, to gain something."Yes, to avoid my fears."No, I haven't."YI am simply enjoying the last of my home. This soothing breeze will the be the last."4Please, you have lived with us for generations!"CYou had to meddle. We have lost our traditions because of you!"I cannot let this happen!"You must have a plan!Iu;␀�[[#"3Thank you for listening to me and coming here."	\PN!",Are you sure you aren’t Psychic-type?"jI spent the last day mulling over whether to call you, and here you are, arriving of your own accord."<…I’m glad to see you, even if part of me isn’t…"#Let’s get right to business."@You probably figured this out already, but I’m ex- Chasm."eA few years ago I joined an expedition into the Circuit Cave organized by the Makyan Government."TOur goal: to understand the circuitry and machinery housed in the lower layers."rAs it turns out, being the only engineer in a throng of useless academics makes it hard to get anything done."~Who cares about “cultural significance” or “hydrological processes" when we don’t even know what the thing does?!"*…but that’s all in the past, now."AI brought you here because of a different group of ex-Chasm."The Drillers.""What a lovely bunch they are."hThey’re basically a gang wearing ranger uniforms— and this corner of Makya is their “turf”."dUsually we’re keen to avoid the Regi Tombs, but recent events have… got some of us nervous."`That’s what the Drillers are saying, anyways… that they’re here to protect the place."Keep the prisons secure.",I think that’s a load of Tauros dung."FAnd even if it’s not, I don’t trust them around the machines."~So, my request: Figure out what The Drillers are doing. And stop them, if my instincts about their mission prove correct."#Finish the job that I can’t."!I’ll stand watch out here.";Need a refresher? I know, it’s a lot of informati