er! Looks like they did a little bit of hackerooni.Iu;␀��[[:"HIt's the bottom of a conveyor belt. It'd be impossible to climb up."xFor most of Sweetrock's history, we've relied on Clefable teleportation to get cargo from the factory to the docks."eWe got these conveyor belts installed a few years back, so the cliffside isn't an issue anymore."TWe still have to rely on teleportation to get in and out of the harbor, though."PLooks like the Trainer ahead is moving to block you from going any further."?Do you want to approach them? It looks like a tough fight."1I knew you would arrive, should I only wait."\Excuse the charade – I would prefer my identity remain enshrouded in mystery for now."{All that you are required to understand is who I serve – Yezera. Under her profound guidance, we have achieved our goals."rThe titans have served their purpose. I come then with a simple inquiry: will you not listen to my reasoning?"PThank you. Our goal is naught less than a complete reordering of the world."<My comrades have their own motives, but mine is simple."�The world at present is mercurial and deceptive. Human culture and technology serves as naught but a veil disguising ultimate truth."cOnly the realm of ancient myth, tended by gods, untouched by humans, might let us perceive it."Do you not agree?"/How disappointing, to dismiss it outright."IIf you have no eye for truth, then we have nothing else to speak of."_Forgive me this act of passion, but I expect a titan’s wrath may settle my raging heart."Regirock, heed my command."RTo the contrary: it has adamant support, if only one ruminates on the matter."`Such wavering faith is nigh-useless for my purposes, alas. We require unflinching devotion."_*sigh* I would be forsaking my duty if I did not stall you at the least. Prepare yourself."lI should encourage you to do so. Judge the weight of the world that is against the world that could be."bAlas, I know you will not ruminate idly upon it. You are a threat. That is intolerable to us."UThis shall be no decisive victory of mine, but I cannot let you pass unhindered."/…I should very much like to believe you."`If you speak truth, then I bid you repeat your convictions to Yezera herself next you meet."oShe can see the machinations of your heart more clearly than I. Until then, you remain a trainer, as do I."<My enemy I smite, my ally I train. To either, en garde."LIf you will not listen to my entreaties, then you are beyond salvation."VAlas. Perhaps a titan’s fury will enlighten you to the clarity of the ancients."TG’afternoon. Took your sweet time comin’ to find Yezera 'gain, didn’t ya?"CGot no interest in convincing you. Ain’t much of a preacher."�But I gotta set some ground rules 'fore we fight; establish some things. 'Cause we’re gonna fight. Ain’t no other way to it."SThank you kindly. I ain’t real interested in this cloak- and-dagger charade."I’m with Yezera, always."EListen, I’m only gonna say this once: you oughta hear her out.";Don’t care if you agree with her. Just hear her out."RAnd if you hurt her, I’ll make you wish Mavis stopped after Zain. We clear?"(Cocky li’l brat, ain’t ya? Tsk."uWhat’s so damn infuriating 'bout you is I ain’t just able to whip your sorry hide into submission. Too good."LHow 'bout I try anyhow? Titan’s gotta be good for somethin’, right?",Good. I ain’t 'bout ta repeat myself."BNow, I came here with a job to do, and I’m a reliable sort."]Sorry, kid. Yezera wants some peace 'n' quiet. Regirock, lead us off, will ya darlin’?"VHah. Take it from someone who knows, kid: you ain’t even scratched the surface."AI can make you plenty more miserable if I set my mind to it."zBut, cheer up, kid. I’m 'bout to give ya what you always want: a good fight. Facing a Regi oughta cheer ya up. Heh."RNah, I ain’t about to trust that. Ya don’t know jack about me and Yezera."8Bickering old married couple, that’s what we are."9Want to show me you’re with us? Tell it to Yezera."rFor now, I ain’t too keen on letting you off easy. Sorry. Beating folks into the dirt is my job, after all."CAh, well. Guess no matter how hard I try, old habits die hard."BSpeaking of dying hard – lay down and quit moving, will ya?"PHah. They ain’t never been happy with my way of goin’ about covert ops."@Too rough 'nd tumble. I ain’t built for cloak-and-dagger."iSo, let me tell you straight: you listen to Yezera. You hear her out. And don’t you dare hurt her."KAll I ask. And, uh, I wasn’t just sent here to chit-chat. You ready?"1Hey. Fancy meeting you in a place like this."aOh, don’t look so angry – Regirock and I are here to fight you, but we’ll get to that."RI know you’re more than a pretty face. You’re smart. Care to hear me out?"0Aww. I knew I had a good feeling about you."[How do I explain it… well, I hate to use the word, but modern society is degenerate."_We’re distant from the perfect moment of creation. We’ve kind of taken over the world."UNo respect for our elders – the primordial Pokémon that created the universe."zYezera’s going to reset this world back to its origins. And then humanity will be in the bosom of Arceus once more."kDon’t call me insane. Although I’m sure this arrogant, faithless civilization would use that term."QI’m merely devout, and devotion means making sacrifices. For example: you."EI really do like you, but… we all have to sacrifice sometimes."MGodlike Pokémon are now treated as not much more than beasts of burden."MAvatars are destroyed at will because they’re “threats to humans.”"\The world has lost all respect, the divine essence from creation diluted and destroyed."NAnd since you seem to be no different, I can take some joy in this fight."�Arceus created the world. It is pure, and perfect, and resetting the world back to its original form will let us be pure and perfect too."BI’d like to see myself blessed by the grace of our creator.")I’d like to see you that way, too."In time."CFor now, I’ve been ordered to slow you down. Shall we dance?")Good. I knew I saw something in you."BSome spark of faith. I’m a… very good judge of character."�I’d love to just talk with you for a while, but I was explicitly instructed to stop you. So we’ll fight. Don’t take it personally."Oh. Was I too forward?"HMy emotions tend to get the better of me. I’m almost heartbroken."%Well, I suppose I am a stranger."uFortunately, I’ve been sent to slow you down, so I have a convenient vent for all these feelings of rejection."Hello, friend."FBusiness before pleasure: I have been sent to slow your progress.".To that end, I am accompanied by a titan."XBefore we attend to that, however, may I interest you in a short, frank discussion?"RI would rather like to try to convince you of the legitimacy of our position."Thank you for your time."_Yezera’s goal is to recreate the conditions of the world shortly following its creation."oModern science has attained almost complete understanding and mastery over the world – the modern world."�It cannot, however, understand the past. By reverting existence, we may study the universe from its conception and obtain universal knowledge."#This is the only way to do so."vWithout the reversion, humanity will never attain complete understanding of the universe. It is worth all prices."RNow our time for conversation is up, however. Regirock, please do the honors."AAll persons who attempt to advance civilization should care."HUniversal knowledge is a prerequisite for an all- powerful society."\That is my goal. That is the goal of all science: to know, and to apply that knowledge."\Your ignorance implies discussion will get us nowhere. Let us dispense with such, then."<Knowledge will be retained into the new primordial era."8We can rebuild at least small enclaves of humanity."\From there our analysis and conquest will begin: a new society with absolute knowledge."@And, stemming from this absolute knowledge, absolute power."YConsider it. In the mean time, there is the business I mentioned earlier. Excuse me."|I am glad you have the wisdom to agree. If you should wish to support us in our endeavors, I will be happy to have you."xWe will fight for a more enlightened era. For now, however, I must slow you. Business is business. Let us commence."II find this highly unfortunate. You will be left behind by progress."NIf you would prefer to retain your ignorance, however, I cannot help you.".Prepare yourself. Regirock, if you would."Oh. Hey."IYeah, so, I knew you’d be here. Gym challenger, and, uh, all that."…Welp. This is awkward.";How do I say this… you interested in hearing us out?"bWe’ve kinda got the upper hand, but, y’know, don’t really wanna fight you. Whaddya say?"=Oh. That’s good. Great. Honestly didn’t expect that."HWell, I just figure we’ve done a lot of ordering Pokémon around.">Maybe it’s time to even up the footing a bit, y’know?"8We can all kinda make up for whatever we did wrong."mThe others have their reasons, but, uh, this is mine. Make a world where we can be forgiven. You get it?"(Well – fine. You know what? Fine."dI don’t need your permission, and we certainly don’t need your help. Regirock. Do ‘em in."Z…You so sure? Takes a lot of pushing to train a team that strong in so little time."4But, yeah, no, I get it. Why would you help us?"?Rich brat. Maybe we can beat some responsibility into you."NUh. Don’t really know how to break it to you. You… don’t have time."EFor one, we’ve already just about won. For two – think fast!"*Regirock, sweep ‘em off their feet!"*Oh. Didn’t, uh, really expect that.":Figured you were kind of a stuck-up brat. No offense."=Well, good. Maybe we’ll be side by side one day, yeah?"5But, uh, for now… I’m supposed to fight you."HSo, uh, sorry – ah, what am I saying, we live for this. Ready up."Yeah, I guess that tracks."#Fine. That’s… it’s fine."5I came here to beat the crap out of you anyways."kOdds are Regirock isn’t gonna stick around much longer, so let’s make it count. Try your best, eh?"…Hey."xTsk tsk tsk. I’m not gonna lie to you: I’ve been trying to plan this conversation in my head for the past hour."RBut, um, you kinda interrupted me. So can I just say what I want to tell you?"BWelp. Listen, uh, Makya’s kinda in a weird place right now."]Team Chasm ran roughshod over this whole region and then kinda just… got away with it?"So, uh, yeah, if you ever wanted proof that humans can’t get even the most black-and-white justice right, there you are."KWould’ve been simple to fix that little screw-up. But they didn’t."[So we’re taking the power away from humans, and putting it in the hands of Pokémon."Is it? Is it!"AAm I insane for wanting some damn PUNISHMENT in this world?!"DWell, guess what. If people won’t give me it, I’ll MAKE it.""And I’ve got just the tool!"%It is simple, you – you idiot!"aI can track down every ex-Chasm criminal and haul them up to the courts myself if I have to!"UThey just won’t do anything if I did! So I have to do things personally, yeah?" Sorry. Nothing… personal."	Yes!"MThey’re noble and pure and – and – and they’d never let me down!"/Unlike you! And everyone else around here!"JYou want to see? C’mon. See what kind of justice Pokémon can give!"Oh. Ah-hah."LKinda got myself a bit worked up there… welp, no harm, no foul, yeah?"…Nah, that’s stupid."^I’m not gonna waste this chance. I’ve got a Regi. You’re a prodigy. Let’s RUMBLE!"Urgh, you make me so mad!")Nobody will frickin’ listen to me!"
Fine."Y’know, fine, whatever."?You get what everyone else I fight gets. What you deserve."?Regirock – your watch is over. If you would go, then go."YSo it returns to its resting place… no matter. It has done all I desired and more."%As for you, we shall meet again."YFarewell, and do not pursue me. Fate and fate alone will dictate when we next speak."eRegirock’s damn well spent. Flighty li'l things never like to be outside their tombs too long."*Ah, well. Got what I came for anyhow."�Let me tell you one last word of advice. You hurt Yez, I’ll find you. And it won’t just be for some play fight with animals."jG’evening, kid. I’ll see ya around. Make sure I don’t hafta hurt you too bad when I do, ‘kay?";Au revoir, Regirock. Enjoy your entombment, I suppose."PAnd as for you, that was an exciting fight. You’ve got my heart pounding."yIf you want to join us, come find Yezera. And if not, well, we’ll meet again. I’m looking forward to it already."So long."4I surmise Regirock will now return to its tomb."gThe titans are temperamental and ill-suited to existence outside their crypts. It is of no matter."AWe have all but succeeded in our plans. This was a courtesy."7I will take my leave now. Thank you for your time."/There it goes. Back to where it came from."_Well, didn’t really expect to win anyways. Just wanted to slow you down, and, uh, I did.":So… bye. We’ll do this again sometime. I’m out."P*sigh* Buh-bye, Regirock. We don’t really, uh, need you anymore, I guess."?It was fun while it lasted… welp. Nothing lasts forever."ISpeaking of! Hopefully next time we talk it’ll be in a fair world!"KIf it isn’t, then, uh, I’ll give you a run for your money, ‘kay?"\Toodles. And don’t you dare follow – I’m playing hard to get, so respect it. Hah!"uMore than a million years ago, a meteor struck this area of Makya, plowing through a large mountain to the west."XThat large mountain became two smaller mountains, which we now know as Split Peaks."NThe impact site itself would fill with water and become Sweetrock Harbor."0The ocean to the east brings calming winds."KBut why? We might explain it with ocean currents, or weather patterns."FBut what makes the winds here calming? Of that, I am not so sure." Sweetrock Elementary School"/"In loving memory of Mrs. and Mr. Diakos.""HI've been biking across the entire region over the past few months.":Crossing the Split Peaks was by far the hardest part."nThe view from these cliffs, and the feeling that I've finally accomplished my goal, made it all worth it."West: Split Peaks"South: Sandstone Estuary";"Sweetrock Harbor, satisfying the world's sweettooth!""!"A sister city of Canalave!"":I work at Sweetrock Candy factory, like many in town."IThat said, I rarely get to see Victoire, the manager and gym leader.":I gotta rely on rumors to know what her team is like."YAn Aggron that packs a nasty ability, and a Mismagius that's surprisingly resilient."UAlso a Pokemon that's supposed to be... an ice cream cone? I don't get that one."�Her team is unusual, but she must know what she's doing-- At least once a day I see some sorry challenger shuffling out of her office."$Huh, you really beat her, then?"4You gotta tell me what she's like as a trainer.""My curiosity's grown too big!"_Sweetrock Candy is sent all over the world, but more than 30% ends up in the Galar Region."#Those people love their candy.")How goes your journey, young master?"YI've purchased a Clefable teleportation license, and reserved this pier for our use.":We can travel to and from any of our usual locations."Where will we be heading?"Sweetrock Harbor Gym"Leader: Victoire"The Candy Queen!"4Shore leave is always a good time for battling."QNot to mention it keeps me from thinking about post- teleportation nausea...")Do me a favor by having a battle eh?"HAye, no harm no foul. I'll be here waiting if you change your mind."That's the spirit!";A heated moment of battling always soothes the nerves."2Come again if you find yourself by the docks."SMy Pokemon need a bit of rest right now. Come by later for another battle, eh?"Sweetrock Candy Outlet"Sweetrock Lighthouse"#Today's a good day for gaming."Berry Greenhouse"HI love to slide down the conveyor belt. But, my dad doesn't let me."UI have to stay by the school until he gets off work so I don't get into trouble."I'm gaming over here!"No."	Yes."I’ll listen."Don't need it."No, I don't."That's tenuous."I'll think about it."
