, such magnificent power, such… oh, words fail me."HBut it is a little convenient, isn’t it? The two of us come here."LI, the sensitive soul, the pilgrim, and you, the knight, the protector.";And what should we find but a Gallade and a Gardevoir."rMaybe so, maybe not. In any case, I’m glad I had you walk upstairs first, and I hope you enjoyed the brawl."}I honestly envy you. You get to see these avatars up close and truly interact with them. All I can do is view them from afar."mSo it would seem. Appearing in the same biome as their regular counterparts makes sense at first glance."`But even that – how do they choose? Do they choose? Or are they pulled here by something?"OAnd if so, where were they before they were pulled here? If only I knew…"pPerhaps I did. Not intentionally, but, well, maybe that’s how I view us. Relationship goals or something."�And somehow that called them, or created them. If so, I’m deeply sorry – I didn’t intend for you to brawl on my behalf today."hAnd thank you. If you hadn’t showed up, that Gallade might’ve decided I had one too many limbs." Oh, I can make up for this."jWell, what do I know – you probably think an opportunity to fight these things is a gift in itself."IBut in case that doesn’t count as me repaying you, have this back."VIt’s told me what I wanted to know – findings I’ll share with you sometime."MI also happened upon this by pure luck while exploring the deep marshes."0It isn’t much, but I want you to have it."LI know this wasn’t exactly what I promised, but I enjoyed it anyways."oI hope you did too, and I’ll see you around. I’ll make it back to you. I promise. Until we meet again."Coincidence."It isn't random?"Did you call them?["UAsí que sí era un avatar después de todo. ¡Dos, de hecho! ¡Qué encantador!"WTanta gracia, tan magnífico poder, tan… oh, las palabras no les hacen justicia."NPero es un poco conveniente, ¿No? Que nosotros dos hayamos venido aquí."LYo, el alma sensitiva, el peregrino, y tú, el caballero, el p