g is idiocy?"&Sorry – I’m still an asshole."_And that’s your right. It’s your life, and, well, more than one way to skin a Liepard."7I promise I’ll give you a fight worth the title.";Wouldn’t want you to. This isn’t a practice match."5This is the real thing. I’m going to enjoy it."Oh, no, we do."rIt’s fun. It’s fun and it’s a way to wrap this whole thing up. Closure’s stupid but it’s important."N…I know Mavis is going to be watching our duel. Makes me a little sick."TDon’t want it to be tainted by knowing I’m supposed to be "proving myself.""cNothing for it, though. One last battle? I’m not going to lose this one like all the others."_I’m going to lose it in my own way. Hah! Show me what you got, \PN. Show me who you are."0…It feels good to feel good after a loss."DCongratulations. You’re the Champion. Pretty big achievement."WI know your job isn’t exactly over – I don’t have my head stuck in the sand."[As your rival and as your opponent, good game. You beat me fair and square. Great job."PAs your brother, goodbye. I’m not gonna see you again for a little while."fI’m blocking Mavis on everything, picking a direction, and walking until I find something cool.""Thanks. Good luck to you too."SI’d stay, but I’ve got faith you’ve got this whole fiasco under control."7Gonna get a headstart on finding inner peace. Hah."Don’t flatter me.">It’s irresponsible... but, yeah, I need some time away."*I hope you can do the same, honestly."HGet away from Mavis, from the gyms, everything. It’d do you good."!Can’t change my mind, kid."YScrew Mavis. Screw the company. Screw the gyms, screw the Championship, screw Makya."Gonna go find out what I’m actually interested in, 'stead of just trying to one-up you for mommy. But thanks for the concern."Don’t. Seriously."yI know she’s our mom, but she’s the reason we’ve been at each other’s throats. Or, uh, I’ve been at yours."hI’m getting away from her. She wants to talk, she can start by not pitting us against each other."#…It is what it 