"0A locked door. It has a slot for a keycard."'You insert the Team Chasm ID Card."#The door unlocks with a click."It's a vending machine!",However, it no longer holds any drinks.0Iu;␀Ae[[�"Are you ready?";You arrive even here undeterred… but not unforeseen."uYou have heeded Yezera’s invitation even should it bring you into the most dismal abysm of this entire region."wDo you fancy yourself a hero? Do you bear a grudge? Or are you enamored with the idea of facing a former Champion?"IPray, do not tell me. I would delight in divining the answer myself."TI fear I must. Yezera may have invited you, but I extended no such hospitality."EYou two may have your rendezvous in a world of primordial truth."+Now, allow me to peer into your heart."eI shan’t allow you to continue a step further. A world unveiled by mortal deception awaits me."7I will not permit you to deny me my enlightenment."DShall we commence with the inevitable? I grow weary of waiting."YThe hearts and minds of humans are trivial to decipher – with my acumen, at least."UEven discounting my auguries, the soul of a true Trainer is laid bare in battle."+Show me what passion drives you, hero."8Do you take my idiolect for the mark of pretension?"~As you please. Dismiss my words as insipid or overwrought as you wish – I have no need to converse with you any longer."AShall we speak in your native tongue? I am more than fluent."RYou’re late, kid. Ain’t got no manners, keepin' a lady waitin' like that."5Hah! Ain’t talkin' 'bout myself – meant Yez."qDon'tcha gimme that smile. She’s right fine when she’s dolled up, and more than that, she’s my friend."5You’re gonna give her your respect, y'hear me?"xNow, got some bad news for ya: I ain’t lettin' you have your last dance with her if I can help it. This ends now."OGlad to hear ya hearin' me. Now, kid, I ain’t 'bout to pull any punches."L'Cause you’re sweet and oh-so-polite, I ain’t gonna break anything."~But you’re picking’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put ‘em up, kid."6Ah, you’re such a babyface. Real cute one, too."nKinda kid you take home to meet your parents, y’know? Shame I’m gonna have to put you six feet under.">Hah! I kid, I kid – I ain’t doin’ wetwork. Anymore."OI ain’t lettin’ you get away without a few bruises, though. Ready? Go!"LHey – listen, she’s – don’tcha try goin’ and flusterin’ me."gHad to haul that girl to prom, mind ya, and she wears a nice dress a mite better than yours truly."XMy point is that’s she’s a right fine lady, and ya better respect her like one."IAgh, ya got me distracted. Quit with the psyops and fight me proper."WHah! Whatever you say, kid. I ain’t 'bout to take that metaphor and run with it."\You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliche but that’s my line about it."?I guess ya could say I’m reserving the first dance. Hah!"AI like you, kid. C’mere. Lemme beat that humor out of you."�Hello there. You arrived just a teensy bit earlier than I expected – I was writing a poem, see. Never to be finished, tragically."�These black arches of stone like a starless sky will soon be replaced by brilliant alabaster, which, well, ruins the central symbolism."GWhat a shame. I assume you’re going to force me to duel you now?"UYou march into my demesne, hauling your well- trained combat creatures with you."�We’ve fought before. You’re completely opposed to my beautiful dream. And you still want to claim I have a choice in the matter?"aDon’t insult me. You’ve made your choice, and now we have to deal with the consequences."]Ah, well. At least you’re honest. I like that about you. You’ve got such... clarity."�What a gleaming light in this dreary cave. Why, that could almost be poetic! If only we had a hopeless romantic to write that down."QAlas, I’ll be too busy directing my passions into carving your team apart."\Of course! You’re such a brilliant spark in this region. You deserve odes... sonnets."�On the other hand, the fact that you’re here now against me instead of alongside me means that you’re not as special as I thought."MNo faith. It’s a shame, really! I don’t want to do this! But I will."4And, since I have to... might as well enjoy it."JWhat? You think a poetic soul is creepy? Does true faith disturb you?"MGenuine emotions uncompromised by the endless drudgery of society? Fine!"UEnjoy where that narrow-minded view gets you. Namely: here, about to lose to me."Hello, friend."DWe have already begun. Regigigas will quickly remake the world."[I understand that you are here to face Yezera, but unfortunately I can’t allow that."�There is a non-zero chance of your success, and I am not a gambler. If you would like, we can both stay here and talk until the reversion overtakes us."FI supposed as much. Excuse me, but in that case I must fight you."gUniversal knowledge is approaching. I would like to be there to witness it – alone, if possible."cI do not either. Unfortunately, I can tell from your tone that we are, in fact, about to duel."zI am unwilling to let you go further, and I am unwilling to lose. Please understand... and please consider conceding."QThat is the most I am willing to say pertaining to your odds against Yezera."�She is conventionally regarded as unbeatable when she applies herself, though I am aware that you have broken that convention repeatedly."INow, may we end the discussion of theory and add another data point?"OExcuse my verbosity. If you would like to go straight to our duel, we can."gI would not insult your intelligence by pretending we will not fight. That much should be evident."Shall we?"=Oh, uh, hey. Listen: I’m gonna cut right to the chase."2You beat me once. You beat Yezera, um, a lot."mThough, some of those don’t really count, 'cause she was using someone else’s team and – whatever."`Point is, I can’t beat you. But… I gotta try. I’ve got a lot to answer for, y’know?"\Lotta little things I did that I got to make up for. Can’t you just let me have this?"BOf course you can’t. Can’t let me have anything, can you?"bUgh, I was gonna be Champion! I was really gunning for it, too. And then... yeah. Everything."dYou completely overshadow me in every way. I can’t beat you. But I’m gonna try to hurt you."bMaybe to you. But not to them – not to Pokémon. They’re the ones who have to forgive me."~It’s time for them to stop taking orders and start being treated like equals. That includes from ace trainers like you."_I know you can’t stand that, so... I guess we gotta fight. Sorry... but I’m not sorry."-I don’t. Not most of the time anyways."jI’m trying my best to make things right. Can you say the same? Going around keeping the status quo?"hIs this the world you want? I guess you’re a rich brat, so... yeah. Life’s easy, life’s good."IHmph. I’m gonna try and make it a little harder for you, if I can."+Sorry. Guess I’m a spiteful bastard."xNo! I’ll fail – I’ll gladly fail – but I’m not about to give up. I’ve got friends that need protecting."cI’ve got stuff in my past I need to make up for. And I’ve got a world that needs building."A better one – one that’s more equal, more fair. Sorry it isn’t what you want, but I won’t just roll over for you."You ready?"%...Hey. So, uh, this is it, huh?"]You’re, like, not gonna have a change of mind? No justice? No fairness? No punishment?"~Oh, who am I kidding – you’re Tamarind’s lapdog. You’ve been doing her dirty work since, like, literally day one!"8Guess what that means! That’s right: time to pay!"zThat’s what they all said. You’re not a team grunt! You’re just, like, a temporarily inconvenienced mastermind!"dUgh, you’re all the same. Well, I’ve chewed through a lotta grunts. No different this time!"'Nope! But I really really want to!"zTamarind’s out of my reach, but you’re, like, the second-best thing. So c’mere so I can give you a bloody nose."7If you were sorry you’d stop fighting me, idiot!"�You’re such a – such a dolt! How can I get it through your thick skull that you’re the bad guy? Can I beat it into you? Wanna find out?"�Oh, I swear, I’ll roll up these sleeves and deck you myself if I have to! I swear, if you chip my nails I’m gonna kill you for real!"=C’mon, boys and girls! We’ve got a beatdown to give!"Ah. Hah. Hahaha!"}So be it! My reading is complete – the scars of this battle left in the ancient stone here are a portent of things to come."TCan you suppose what it says? It says I shall lose here, and you shall triumph.".Hah! Fate has a sense of humor, it seems."`Go on. Continue yet deeper. I know my place, and will not stand against destiny any longer."qFor my sanity, I will refrain from attempting to divine the results of your future battles. I take my leave."%Awww, kid, you shouldn’t have."xGoin’ all-out? On yours truly? I’m touched. Not even half-honest, either – it’s a treat seein’ you fight."~Go on. Yez is waitin’ for you. I ain’t too hung up on this whole scheme. Yez’ll turn out fine either way – tough girl."RTougher than me, I swear. So you go do what ya got planned, whatever that is."WIf ya hurt her, they’ll never find the body, blah blah blah, you know the drill."AGood luck, kid. Come find me some time afterwards, y’hear?"0...Go. Leave. Now, before I lose my temper."dIs that really what the fate of the universe hangs on? Our relative skill in training Pokémon?"fIt’s ridiculous! It’s idiotic! I can’t believe – go! Just go! I should... I should... go."~Noted. Excuse me – I fear I may not have provided adequate resistance. I now find myself lacking any means to challenge you."m...Understood. I have no recourse but to retreat. I wish you the worst of luck in your future endeavors."KIf you will permit me to leave, I will no longer impede your progress."4Goodbye, friend. I hope never to see you again."Damn it. Damn it!"UI – yeah, that’s how it goes. Never was as good as you. Any of you hotshots."gPushed my Pokémon hard to try and get there, and now look at me. Trying to make up for all of it.":Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Manaphy. I guess that was it."VLet’s get y’all back to a Pokécenter, OK? Get you fixed up... I’m sorry..."AUgh! I’m – fine! Ow. I think I took a stray shot... oof."�Look me in the damn eyes, you dumb grunt! If I was – ow – if I wasn’t... if I wasn’t... I’m feeling a little lightheaded."RIs this why they black out after losing...? I’m gonna... I can’t do this."fGo do whatever it is you think you’re, like, actually accomplishing. You stupid, stupid dolt..."{But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put 'em up, kid."]You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliché but that’s my line about it.")I should’ve known she was useless."jYezera was THIS close. So close to getting everything she wanted. All she had to do was not tell you."}She had to not be human. Her one redeeming quality: her inhumanity. And now she went and betrayed that, and with it, me."0Apparently. It’s sickening, to be honest."tThe same shallow, stupid desires as everyone else. I guess I’m just as much of an idiot for believing in her."Yes. Good. For. Her."fUnfortunately, it isn’t so good for her grand plan, nor mine. I hope the catharsis is worth it."5Yes, she did. I’m glad you’ve realized that."(Fine. I hope I never see you again."HBut, well, I’ll take care of her once the regression is complete.";You, on the other hand, I’ll deal with now. So long."XDo you want me to dispose of your team again? Go on ahead. I can delay you all day."No!"#I want it! I want it so badly!"EI’d – you don’t understand. You don’t understand at all."(How sickened I am at you creatures.".Fine. You win. Go rendezvous with Yezera."'I hope she puts you in your place."AIf you ever see me again, it won’t end well for one of us."&I'm getting the hell out of here."No."	Yes."You stopping me?"Get out of my way."You think you can?"Please, just shut up."Yeah, it does."Don't wanna do this.""Dolled up?""I'll dance if I want to."Not forcing you."Yeah, I am."A poem? For me?"Still creepy, huh?"Not happening."Don't want to fight."Wait, "non-zero?""Talked too long already."No, I can't."This is wrong."Don't hate yourself."Just give up."I'm not her lapdog."Do we have to?"Sorry."Fine, bring it on."She's human."Good for her."Yeah, she did."!Shut up. For good this time."}But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put ‘em up, kid.[�"¿Estás listo?"DLlegaste incluso aquí decidido… pero no es ninguna sorpresa."mHas acatado la invitación de Yezera incluso si te trayera al abismo más lúgubre de toda esta región."~¿Te ves a ti mismo como un héroe? ¿Acaso guardas un rencor? ¿O te enamora la idea de enfrentar a un antiguo Campeón?"VNo es necesario que me digas. Me deleitaría adivinar la respuesta por mi cuenta."cMe temo que no tengo opción. Yezera pudo haberte invitado, pero yo no daré tal hospitalidad."QEspero que ustedes dos tengan su encuentro en un mundo de verdad primordial.",Ahora, permíteme observar tu corazón."bNo te permítere dar otro paso en frente. Un mundo desvelado por un engaño mortal me espera."1No permitire que me niegues mi iluminación."B¿Comenzamos con lo inevitable? Me estoy cansando de esperar."kLos corazones y mentes de los humanos son triviales de descifrar – con mi perspicacia, por lo menos."`Incluso sin contar mis augurios, el alma de un verdadero Entrenador es exhibida en combate."0Muéstrame qué pasión te impulsa, héroe.":¿Tomas mi idiolecto como una muestra de pretensión?"�Como quieras. Desestima mis palabras como insípidas o recargadas como desees – no tengo necesidad de conversar contigo por más tiempo."G¿Mejor hablamos en tu lengua nativa? Soy bastante fluido en ella."[Llegas tarde, niño. No tienes modales, haciendo esperar a una señorita de esa forma."0¡Ja! No hablo de mi – me refería a Yez."lNo sonrías de esa forma. Ella está muy bien cuando está arreglada, y más que eso, ella es mi amiga."'Y vas a respetarla, ¿Me escuchas?"�Ahora, tengo un par de malas noticias para ti: no voy a dejar que tengas tu último baile con ella si puedo intervenir. Esto termina ahora."PMe alegra que estés escuchando. Ahora, niño, no voy a irme con chiquitas."<Porque eres taan dulce y educado, no voy a romper nada."{Pero estás eligiendo una pelea con Yez, así que te voy a dejar con un par de moratones. ¿Listo? Ve con todo, niño."3Ah, tienes tal cara de bebé. Y una tan linda."�El tipo de niño que llevas a tu casa a que conozca a tus padres, ¿Sabes? Lástima que te tenga que enterrar un par de metros bajo el suelo."F¡Ja! Es broma, es broma – ya no hago ese trabajo sucio. Ya no."LNo voy a dejarte ir sin un par de moretones, eso sí. ¿Listo? ¡Vamos!">Hey – escucha, ella – para de intentar ir y agitarme."sTuve que llevar esa niña al baile, y para que sepas, ella usa un buen vestido un poco mejor que su servidora."YMi punto es que ella es una buena señorita, y será mejor que la respetes como una."JAgh, me distraíste. Deja los juegos mentales y lucha apropiadamente."O¡Ja! Lo que digas, niño. No voy a tomar esa metáfora y seguir con ella."wQuieres llegar a ella, tienes que pasar sobre mi. Llámame cliché pero eso es lo que tengo que decir al respecto."KSupongo que podrías decir que estoy reservando el primer baile. ¡Ja!"<Me gustas, niño. Déjame quitarte ese humor a fuerzas."�Buenas. Llegaste un tanto más temprano de lo que esperaba – estaba escribiendo un poema, sabes. Uno que nunca será terminado, trágicamente."�Estos arcos de piedra negra como un cielo sin estrellas pronto será reemplazado por un alabastro brillante, que, bueno, arruinan el simbolismo central."GQué lástima. ¿Asumo que me forzarás en un duelo contigo ahora?"\Marchas hacia mi tenencia, arrastrando tus bienentrenadas criaturas de combate contigo."�Hemos combatido antes. Eres lo completamente opuesto a mi maravilloso sueño. ¿Y aún asi clamas que tengo elección en el asunto?"[No me insultes. Hiciste tu decisión, y ahora tienes que lidiar con las consecuencias."VAh, bueno. Por lo menos eres honesto. Me gusta eso de ti. Tienes tal… claridad."�Una luz brillante en esta cueva sombría. ¡Esto está a nada de ser poético! Si tan solo tuvieramos un romántico sin remedio para escribirlo."WLástima, estaré muy ocupada concentrando mis pasiones en desmenuzar a tu equipo."_¡Por supuesto! Eres tan brillante chispa en esta región. Te mereces una oda…un soneto."�Por otro lado, el hecho de que estas aquí y ahora en contra de mi en vez de a mi lado significa que no eres tan especial como pensé."USin lealtad. ¡En serio, es una lástima! ¡No quiero hacer esto! Pero lo haré."=Y, ya que tengo que hacerlo… más me vale disfrutarlo."]¿Qué? ¿Crees que un alma poética da miedo? ¿Acaso la verdadera lealtad te inquieta?"g¿Emociones genuinas que se mantienen intactas por la monotonía sin fin de esta sociedad? ¡Bien!"nDisfruta donde esa perspectiva estrecha va a llevarte. Concretamente: aquí, A punto de perder contra mi."Hola, amigo."FYa hemos comenzado. Regigigas enseguida volvera a crear el mundo."gEntiendo que estés quí para enfrentarte a Yezera, pero desafortunadamente no puedo permitir eso."�La probabilidad de que ganes no es nula, y no soy un apostador. Si lo prefieres, podemos quedarnos aquí y hablar hasta que la reversión llegue a nosotros."FEso supuse. Disculpame, pero en ese caso debo combatir contra ti."wEl conocimiento universal se acerca. Y me gustaría estar aquí para presenciarlo – en solitario, si es posible."tTampoco lo hago. Desafortunadamente, puedo decir por el tono en que estamos en que, de hecho, vamos a combatir."{No estoy dispuesto a dejarte ir más allá, y tampoco lo estoy a perder. Por favor entiende… y por favor considera ceder."WEso es lo más que estoy dispuesto a decir sobre tus propabilidades contra Yezera."�Ella es convencionalmente considerada invencible cuando se concentra, aunque soy consciente que has roto esta costumbre repetidamente."[Ahora, ¿Y si terminamos esta discusión sobre teoría y añadimos otro punto de dato?"SExcusa mi verborrea. Si preferies ir directo a nuestro duelo, podemos hacerlo."hNo quisiera insultar tu inteligencia pretendiendo que no vamos a luchar. Eso debería ser evidente."¿Empezamos?"-Oh, eh, hey. Escucha: voy a ir al grano.">Me derrotaste una vez. Y derrotaste a Yezera, em, varias."vAunque, algunas de esas realmente no cuentan, ya que ella estaba usando el equipo de alguien más y – como sea."fEl punto es, no puedo vencerte. Pero… tengo que intentarlo. Tengo mucho que responder, ¿Sabes?"lUn montón de pequeñas cosas que hice que tengo que compensar. ¿No me puedes dejar por lo menos esto?"@Por supuesto que no puedes. No puedes dejar nada, ¿Cierto?"dUgh, ¡Iba a ser el Campeón! Realmente estaba apuntando a eso, en serio. Y luego… seh. Todo."SMe eclipsas de cada manera. No puedo vencerte. Pero voy a intentar lastimarte."fQuizás para ti. Pero no ellos – no para los Pokémon. Ellos son los que tienen que perdonarme."�Es hora de que dejen de seguir órdenes y empieces a ser tratados como iguales. Eso incluye a los entrenadores “estrella” como tú."pSé que no puedes soportarlo, así que… supongo que tenemos que combatir. Lo siento… pero no lo siento."8No lo hago. No la mayoría del tiempo por lo menos."|Estoy intentando lo mejor posible para enmendar las cosas. ¿Puedes decir lo mismo? ¿Ir por ahí manteniendo el status quo?"}¿Este es el mundo que quieres? Supongo que eres un mocoso malcriado… así que… seh. La vida es fácil, la vida es buena."NHmph. Voy a intentarlo y hacerlo un poco más difícil para ti, si puedo."6Lo siento. Supongo que soy un bastardo rencoroso."v¡No! Voy a fallar – con gusto lo haré – pero no me voy a rendir. Tengo amigos que necesitan ser protegidos."cTengo cosas en mi pasado que tengo que enmendar. Y tengo un mundo que necesita ser construido."sUno mejor – uno más equitativo, más justo. Perdón si no es lo que querías, pero no voy a someterme a ti."¿Listo?"* ...Hey. Así que, eh, así es, ¿Eh?"b¿Ya no vas a tener, sabes, un cambio de opinión? ¿No justicia? ¿No equidad? ¿No castigo?"�Oh, a quién quiero engañar – eres el perrito faldero de Tamarind. Has estado haciendo su trabajo sucio desde, como, ¡Literalmente día uno!">¡Adivina lo que eso significa! ¡Así es: hora de pagar!"uEso es lo que todos dicen. ¡No eres un recluta! ¡Sólo eres, como, una mente maestra temporalmente incomodada!"tUgh, ustedes son siempre lo mismo. Bueno, he masticado un montón de reclutas. ¡Y esta vez no será diferente!"-¡Nope! ¡Pero realmente quiero hacerlo!"�Tamarind está fuera de mi alcance, pero tu eres, como, la segunda mejor opción. Así que ven aquí para que te rompa la nariz."G¡Si lo dijeras de verdad dejarías de combatir contra mi, idiota!"�¡Eres tan – tan bobo! ¿Cómo se supone que te haga entender que eres el tipo malo? ¿Puede vencerte para hacerlo? ¿Quierés que lo intentemos?"�Oh, te lo juro, ¡Me subiría las mangas y te tumbaría por mi cuenta si tengo que hacerlo! ¡Te lo juro, si me molestas, te voy a matar de verdad!"<¡Vamos, chicos y chicas! ¡Tenemos una paliza que dar!"Ah. Ja. ¡Jajaja!"�¡Que así sea! Mi lectura está completa – las cicatrices de este combate dejadas en la piedra antigua son un augurio de lo que se viene."U¿Puedes suponer lo que dice? Dice que perderé aquí, y tú saldras victorioso."<¡Ja! Parece que el destino tiene un sentido del humor."iSigue. Continúa aún más, conozco mi lugar, y no me pararé en contra del destino por más tiempo."nPor mi sanidad, me abstendré de intentar adivinar el resultado de tus combates futuros. Ahora me retiro."-Awww, niño, no deberías haberlo hecho."{¿Ir con todo? ¿Contra su servidor? Me conmueves. Tampoco estoy diciendo verdades a medias – es un gusto verte combatir."Sigue. Yez te está esperando. No me preocupa demasiado todo esto. Yez va a estar bien de cualquier modo – es una chica dura."YMás dura que yo, lo juro. Así que ve y haz lo que tengas planeado, sea lo que sea."YSi la lastima, nunca encontrarán el cuerpo, bla bla bla, ya sabes cómo es el tema."IBuena suerte, chico. Encuéntrame cuando tengas tiempo, ¿Entendido?"=…Ve. Vete. Ahora, antes de que pierda mi temperamento."t¿Es realmente de eso lo que depende el destino del universo? ¿Nuestra habilidad relativa entrenando Pokémon?"o¡Es rídiculo! ¡Es una idiotez! ¡No puedo creerlo – vete! ¡Sólo vete! Debería… debería… irme."}Entendido. Discúlpame – temo que no pude proveer una resistencia adecuada.  Ahora me encuentro sin medios para desafiarte."q...Entendido. No tengo más remedio que retirarme. Te deseo la peor de las suertes en tus futuros esfuerzos."6Si me permites irme, ya no impediré tu progreso."/Adiós, amigo. Espero no verte nunca más." Maldita sea. ¡Maldita sea!"\Entonces – seh, así es como es. Siempre fui peor que tú. Que cualquiera de ustedes."eEmpujé a mis Pokémon demasiado para llegar allí, y ahora mírame. Intentando enmendarlo todo."FLo siento, a todos. Lo siento, Manaphy. Supongo que eso fue todo."VVayamos a un Centro Pokémon, ¿Ok? Para que vuelvan a estar bien… lo siento…"H¡Ugh! ¡Estoy – bien! Au. Creo que tomé una bala perdida… uf."{Mírame a los malditos ojos, ¡Tonto recluta! Si fuera – ow – si no fuera… si no fuera… me siento un poco aturdida."T¿Es por esto que se desmayan luego de perder…? Voy a… no puedo hacer esto."eHaz lo que quieras si crees que es, como, un logro de verdad. Estúpido, estúpido bobalicón…"~Pero estás eligiendo un combate con Yez, así que te voy a dejar con un par de moretones. ¿Estás listo? Vamos a ello chico."fSi quieres llegar a ella, debes pasar sobre mi. Llámame cliché pero es lo que digo al respecto."4Debería haber sabido que ella era una inútil."{Yezera estaba ASÍ de cerca. Tan cerca de tener todo lo que ella quería. Todo lo que tenía que hacer era no decirte."yTenía que no ser humana. Su única cualidad redimible: su inhumanidad. Y ahora va y la traiciona, y con ello, a mi."-Aparentemente. Es repugnante, la verdad."tLos mismos deseos superficiales y estúpidos que todos los demás. Supongo que soy igual de idiota por creerle."Sí. Bien. Por. Ella."iDesafortunadamente, no es muy buena para su gran plan, ni el mío. Espero que la catársis lo valga."6Sí, lo hizo. Me alegra que te hayas dado cuenta."$Bien. Espero no volverte a ver."OPero, bueno, ya me encargaré de ella cuando la regresión esté completa.":De ti, por el otro lado, me encargaré ahora. Adiós."Z¿Quieres que me deshaga de tu equipo de nuevo? Vamos. Puedo retrasarte todo el día."
¡No!"(¡Lo quiero! ¡Realmente lo quiero!"9No – no lo entiendes. No lo entiendes en absoluto."+Lo enfermo que estoy de todos ustedes."2Bien. Tú ganas. Ten tu encuentro con Yezera."%Espero que te ponga en su lugar."MSi algún día me ves de nuevo, no terminará bien para uno de nosotros." Me voy al demonio de aquí."No."	Sí."¿Me estás deteniendo?"Fuera de mi camino." ¿Crees que puedes hacerlo?"Por favor, cállate."Seh, lo hace."No quiero hacer esto.""¿Arreglada?""Bailaré si quieres."No te voy a forzar."Sí, lo hago/soy."¿Un poema? ¿Para mi?"¿Aún espeluznante, eh?"No va a ocurrir."No quiero combatir." Espera, ”¿No es nula?”"Ya hablaste demasiado."No, no puedo."Esto está mal."No te odies."Sólo ríndete."No soy su perro faldero."¿Tenemos que hacerlo?"Lo siento."Bien, vamos a ello."Ella es humana."Bien por ella."Seh, lo hizo."$Cállate. De una vez por todas."rPero estás eligiendo un combate con Yez, así que te dejaré algunos moretones. ¿Listo? Vamos allá, chico.;[�"Are you ready?";You arrive even here undeterred… but not unforeseen."uYou have heeded Yezera’s invitation even should it bring you into the most dismal abysm of this entire region."wDo you fancy yourself a hero? Do you bear a grudge? Or are you enamored with the idea of facing a former Champion?"IPray, do not tell me. I would delight in divining the answer myself."TI fear I must. Yezera may have invited you, but I extended no such hospitality."EYou two may have your rendezvous in a world of primordial truth."+Now, allow me to peer into your heart."eI shan’t allow you to continue a step further. A world unveiled by mortal deception awaits me."7I will not permit you to deny me my enlightenment."DShall we commence with the inevitable? I grow weary of waiting."YThe hearts and minds of humans are trivial to decipher – with my acumen, at least."UEven discounting my auguries, the soul of a true Trainer is laid bare in battle."+Show me what passion drives you, hero."8Do you take my idiolect for the mark of pretension?"~As you please. Dismiss my words as insipid or overwrought as you wish – I have no need to converse with you any longer."AShall we speak in your native tongue? I am more than fluent."RYou’re late, kid. Ain’t got no manners, keepin' a lady waitin' like that."5Hah! Ain’t talkin' 'bout myself – meant Yez."qDon'tcha gimme that smile. She’s right fine when she’s dolled up, and more than that, she’s my friend."5You’re gonna give her your respect, y'hear me?"xNow, got some bad news for ya: I ain’t lettin' you have your last dance with her if I can help it. This ends now."OGlad to hear ya hearin' me. Now, kid, I ain’t 'bout to pull any punches."L'Cause you’re sweet and oh-so-polite, I ain’t gonna break anything."~But you’re picking’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put ‘em up, kid."6Ah, you’re such a babyface. Real cute one, too."nKinda kid you take home to meet your parents, y’know? Shame I’m gonna have to put you six feet under.">Hah! I kid, I kid – I ain’t doin’ wetwork. Anymore."OI ain’t lettin’ you get away without a few bruises, though. Ready? Go!"LHey – listen, she’s – don’tcha try goin’ and flusterin’ me."gHad to haul that girl to prom, mind ya, and she wears a nice dress a mite better than yours truly."XMy point is that’s she’s a right fine lady, and ya better respect her like one."IAgh, ya got me distracted. Quit with the psyops and fight me proper."WHah! Whatever you say, kid. I ain’t 'bout to take that metaphor and run with it."\You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliche but that’s my line about it."?I guess ya could say I’m reserving the first dance. Hah!"AI like you, kid. C’mere. Lemme beat that humor out of you."�Hello there. You arrived just a teensy bit earlier than I expected – I was writing a poem, see. Never to be finished, tragically."�These black arches of stone like a starless sky will soon be replaced by brilliant alabaster, which, well, ruins the central symbolism."GWhat a shame. I assume you’re going to force me to duel you now?"UYou march into my demesne, hauling your well- trained combat creatures with you."�We’ve fought before. You’re completely opposed to my beautiful dream. And you still want to claim I have a choice in the matter?"aDon’t insult me. You’ve made your choice, and now we have to deal with the consequences."]Ah, well. At least you’re honest. I like that about you. You’ve got such... clarity."�What a gleaming light in this dreary cave. Why, that could almost be poetic! If only we had a hopeless romantic to write that down."QAlas, I’ll be too busy directing my passions into carving your team apart."\Of course! You’re such a brilliant spark in this region. You deserve odes... sonnets."�On the other hand, the fact that you’re here now against me instead of alongside me means that you’re not as special as I thought."MNo faith. It’s a shame, really! I don’t want to do this! But I will."4And, since I have to... might as well enjoy it."JWhat? You think a poetic soul is creepy? Does true faith disturb you?"MGenuine emotions uncompromised by the endless drudgery of society? Fine!"UEnjoy where that narrow-minded view gets you. Namely: here, about to lose to me."Hello, friend."DWe have already begun. Regigigas will quickly remake the world."[I understand that you are here to face Yezera, but unfortunately I can’t allow that."�There is a non-zero chance of your success, and I am not a gambler. If you would like, we can both stay here and talk until the reversion overtakes us."FI supposed as much. Excuse me, but in that case I must fight you."gUniversal knowledge is approaching. I would like to be there to witness it – alone, if possible."cI do not either. Unfortunately, I can tell from your tone that we are, in fact, about to duel."zI am unwilling to let you go further, and I am unwilling to lose. Please understand... and please consider conceding."QThat is the most I am willing to say pertaining to your odds against Yezera."�She is conventionally regarded as unbeatable when she applies herself, though I am aware that you have broken that convention repeatedly."INow, may we end the discussion of theory and add another data point?"OExcuse my verbosity. If you would like to go straight to our duel, we can."gI would not insult your intelligence by pretending we will not fight. That much should be evident."Shall we?"=Oh, uh, hey. Listen: I’m gonna cut right to the chase."2You beat me once. You beat Yezera, um, a lot."mThough, some of those don’t really count, 'cause she was using someone else’s team and – whatever."`Point is, I can’t beat you. But… I gotta try. I’ve got a lot to answer for, y’know?"\Lotta little things I did that I got to make up for. Can’t you just let me have this?"BOf course you can’t. Can’t let me have anything, can you?"bUgh, I was gonna be Champion! I was really gunning for it, too. And then... yeah. Everything."dYou completely overshadow me in every way. I can’t beat you. But I’m gonna try to hurt you."bMaybe to you. But not to them – not to Pokémon. They’re the ones who have to forgive me."~It’s time for them to stop taking orders and start being treated like equals. That includes from ace trainers like you."_I know you can’t stand that, so... I guess we gotta fight. Sorry... but I’m not sorry."-I don’t. Not most of the time anyways."jI’m trying my best to make things right. Can you say the same? Going around keeping the status quo?"hIs this the world you want? I guess you’re a rich brat, so... yeah. Life’s easy, life’s good."IHmph. I’m gonna try and make it a little harder for you, if I can."+Sorry. Guess I’m a spiteful bastard."xNo! I’ll fail – I’ll gladly fail – but I’m not about to give up. I’ve got friends that need protecting."cI’ve got stuff in my past I need to make up for. And I’ve got a world that needs building."A better one – one that’s more equal, more fair. Sorry it isn’t what you want, but I won’t just roll over for you."You ready?"%...Hey. So, uh, this is it, huh?"]You’re, like, not gonna have a change of mind? No justice? No fairness? No punishment?"~Oh, who am I kidding – you’re Tamarind’s lapdog. You’ve been doing her dirty work since, like, literally day one!"8Guess what that means! That’s right: time to pay!"zThat’s what they all said. You’re not a team grunt! You’re just, like, a temporarily inconvenienced mastermind!"dUgh, you’re all the same. Well, I’ve chewed through a lotta grunts. No different this time!"'Nope! But I really really want to!"zTamarind’s out of my reach, but you’re, like, the second-best thing. So c’mere so I can give you a bloody nose."7If you were sorry you’d stop fighting me, idiot!"�You’re such a – such a dolt! How can I get it through your thick skull that you’re the bad guy? Can I beat it into you? Wanna find out?"�Oh, I swear, I’ll roll up these sleeves and deck you myself if I have to! I swear, if you chip my nails I’m gonna kill you for real!"=C’mon, boys and girls! We’ve got a beatdown to give!"Ah. Hah. Hahaha!"}So be it! My reading is complete – the scars of this battle left in the ancient stone here are a portent of things to come."TCan you suppose what it says? It says I shall lose here, and you shall triumph.".Hah! Fate has a sense of humor, it seems."`Go on. Continue yet deeper. I know my place, and will not stand against destiny any longer."qFor my sanity, I will refrain from attempting to divine the results of your future battles. I take my leave."%Awww, kid, you shouldn’t have."xGoin’ all-out? On yours truly? I’m touched. Not even half-honest, either – it’s a treat seein’ you fight."~Go on. Yez is waitin’ for you. I ain’t too hung up on this whole scheme. Yez’ll turn out fine either way – tough girl."RTougher than me, I swear. So you go do what ya got planned, whatever that is."WIf ya hurt her, they’ll never find the body, blah blah blah, you know the drill."AGood luck, kid. Come find me some time afterwards, y’hear?"0...Go. Leave. Now, before I lose my temper."dIs that really what the fate of the universe hangs on? Our relative skill in training Pokémon?"fIt’s ridiculous! It’s idiotic! I can’t believe – go! Just go! I should... I should... go."~Noted. Excuse me – I fear I may not have provided adequate resistance. I now find myself lacking any means to challenge you."m...Understood. I have no recourse but to retreat. I wish you the worst of luck in your future endeavors."KIf you will permit me to leave, I will no longer impede your progress."4Goodbye, friend. I hope never to see you again."Damn it. Damn it!"UI – yeah, that’s how it goes. Never was as good as you. Any of you hotshots."gPushed my Pokémon hard to try and get there, and now look at me. Trying to make up for all of it.":Sorry, everyone. Sorry, Manaphy. I guess that was it."VLet’s get y’all back to a Pokécenter, OK? Get you fixed up... I’m sorry..."AUgh! I’m – fine! Ow. I think I took a stray shot... oof."�Look me in the damn eyes, you dumb grunt! If I was – ow – if I wasn’t... if I wasn’t... I’m feeling a little lightheaded."RIs this why they black out after losing...? I’m gonna... I can’t do this."fGo do whatever it is you think you’re, like, actually accomplishing. You stupid, stupid dolt..."{But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put 'em up, kid."]You want to get to her, ya go through me. Call me cliché but that’s my line about it.")I should’ve known she was useless."jYezera was THIS close. So close to getting everything she wanted. All she had to do was not tell you."}She had to not be human. Her one redeeming quality: her inhumanity. And now she went and betrayed that, and with it, me."0Apparently. It’s sickening, to be honest."tThe same shallow, stupid desires as everyone else. I guess I’m just as much of an idiot for believing in her."Yes. Good. For. Her."fUnfortunately, it isn’t so good for her grand plan, nor mine. I hope the catharsis is worth it."5Yes, she did. I’m glad you’ve realized that."(Fine. I hope I never see you again."HBut, well, I’ll take care of her once the regression is complete.";You, on the other hand, I’ll deal with now. So long."XDo you want me to dispose of your team again? Go on ahead. I can delay you all day."No!"#I want it! I want it so badly!"EI’d – you don’t understand. You don’t understand at all."(How sickened I am at you creatures.".Fine. You win. Go rendezvous with Yezera."'I hope she puts you in your place."AIf you ever see me again, it won’t end well for one of us."&I'm getting the hell out of here."No."	Yes."You stopping me?"Get out of my way."You think you can?"Please, just shut up."Yeah, it does."Don't wanna do this.""Dolled up?""I'll dance if I want to."Not forcing you."Yeah, I am."A poem? For me?"Still creepy, huh?"Not happening."Don't want to fight."Wait, "non-zero?""Talked too long already."No, I can't."This is wrong."Don't hate yourself."Just give up."I'm not her lapdog."Do we have to?"Sorry."Fine, bring it on."She's human."Good for her."Yeah, she did."!Shut up. For good this time."}But you’re pickin’ a fight with Yez, so I’m gonna leave you with some bruises. You 'bout ready? Put ‘em up, kid.0Iu;␀u4[[e"*Multiple candles required for one fog"KJunction blocked by candle. Acts as a battery for flames between rooms"!Doesn't open from this side."^Airlock: Need to spend flame(s) in the top section to retrieve flame(s) in bottom section"Flame after illusory wall"PYezera and the others are gone, I’m afraid. It’s just you… and… me.":We won. No reason for me to be here. Absolutely none."XOther than the immense enjoyment I’m about to extract from dismantling your team."EA friend of Yezera’s. Besides that, I’m masked for a reason."iI would ask who you are, but quite frankly it doesn’t matter. I’m going to find out soon enough."9There’s only so many types of people in the world.":I just told you: because humiliating you will be fun."MUnless you mean extracting Regidrago, in which case, no, I won’t tell."bHumans have this infuriatingly self-destructive need to tell secrets. I’m better than that."3Well, I see the dialogue’s broken down fast."Fine. Suffer."6But I didn’t come here to engage in small talk."iI assure you, it isn’t personal – no one has anything interesting to say. You’re no exception."WBut you are exceptionally skilled, I understand, and that’s correlated with ego."5Allow me to show you what you’re really worth."V…Ah, so be it. I doubt I could drill humility through your thick skull anyways."=You’re good at playing shallow games – good for you."<Ibis, get us out of here. I’ve seen more than enough."hThey got away. They won. A few that were masked, including whoever the hell THAT was. And Yezera…"UWish I knew. That guy was a narcissist and an asshole, I can tell you that much."#The rest of them… who knows."Could be anything."jBut if they were after Regidrago specifically, and Yezera’s with them… maybe even leading them…"4…I don’t know. It doesn’t make any sense.">She should be the last person to pull this kind of stunt."XIt is. It’s your problem now, and I know you aren’t gonna like that, but it is."5This is bigger than just one legendary Pokémon."7I’m gonna let you in on the big open secret, OK?"oThe caves around Makya are tombs for the Regis. The weird ones I was talking about before. Ones like this."NWell, some archaeological teams went to study them a couple decades back."yAnd then they found the Regis, and the rich mineral veins, and the ruins, and they figured they could leverage that."{We got some corporate backing from Andris and Mavis, and boom: Team Chasm. I was one of those original archaeologists."n…Some of us. Helena wanted to run her own region. Andris wanted a piece of the organized crime bigtime."QMe, I study the Regis. And some people wanted me to leave well enough alone."jI had a Team and Regidrago on my side, and they didn’t, so I got to study what I damn well pleased."LSome of us. I didn’t. I had five Regis – what did I need money for?"8If I wanted lab equipment, I sent a list to Helena."GI lived in a research station and ate ramen. Best days of my life."oI just wanted to study the Regis, and with their power, nobody could tell me no. Funny how that works out.")You make it sound so pure and noble."bI was curious. Wanted answers. I got them – who could tell me no with Regidrago at my side?"YNot to mention the full might of Team Chasm, 'cause my research was VERY profitable."QI’m getting to that, but also, hey, it could come in handy some day, yeah?"5As I was saying: we found the five lesser Regis."\It took me years, but I deciphered their inscriptions and understood their true nature."JThat led us to Regigigas, and at that point we were cooking with gas."RGigas was stronger than the rest of the Regis put together, and smarter, too."|Shape the earth, revert it back to some kind of primordial clay. Create seals and wards that nothing could get through."2And, yeah, it could throw a mean Giga Impact."iIt could do… other things, too. We found a way to make it create ethereal Pokémon with its power.";They were hostile, powerful – had to be locked away."}And then by the time Yezera kicked down our door and told us to stop, she was basically just confirming what we already knew."pWe were playing with fire. If we kept using Regigigas, we ran the very real chance of destroying the world."`Or at least permanently changing it. So we put each Regi back in their tomb and went legit."iThe tombs were reinforced, of course – just about nothing can get through the minor Regi chambers."KGigas’s chamber can only be opened by the other five Regis together."_I don’t know. She agreed with us: it was too dangerous. We were criminals, not lunatics."MI know things… haven’t been great for her, but this? This is insane."[Who knows. We knew some groups were trying to get them back – they always have been."PBut succeeding? There was no way. Impossible. But… apparently Yezera can."*…Probably. They might already have."nGigas’s chamber is deep down, though, and if they haven’t broken the seal yet, it’d be for nothing."QOr if they’ve resealed it. I can try and scout it out, but… no promises."^My POINT is that if you don’t help out, you better get used to the look of white stone."]You’re gonna be seeing a whole lot more of it if someone tells Regigigas to let loose."<Listen, I don’t know. I don’t know a lot of things."sSo let me talk to Andris, our rangers, Helena, whoever else I can find. We’ll figure out how bad things are."PAnd if these thieves show their faces aboveground, you can brawl with them."~They’ve got at least one Regi, probably more, so there’s a strong temptation to wreak havoc. Trust me – I’d know."JHate to say it, but you just need to keep being your usual self, kid."JOr, no, I shouldn’t call you kid. Take this – you’ve earned it."AUsed to give these to Chasm strike teams, for cave scouting."UIt’ll get you just about anywhere in the region – nobody hides from you now."3So go get those badges and save the day, hero."jMisleading Airlock\nYou can put a flame in the upper stick to grab the lower one and take it with you"LLit Candle that when taking flame casts shadow somewhere in the dungeon"Who are you?"Why are you doing this?"Shut up, edgelord."Who are they?"What do they want?"Why Yezera?"Not my problem."You wanted power?"You wanted money?"You wanted knowledge?"Why should I care?"Then why is Yezera..."How many Regis are stolen?"They're opening that door."Your point?[e"4Múltiples velas son requeridas para la niebla."iLa unión es bloqueada por la vela. Actúa como una batería para las flamas entre las habitaciones."No abre desde este lado."�Compartimento estanco: Necesitas gastar la(s) llama(s) en la sección superior para retirar la(s) llama(s) en la sección inferior"*La llama luego de una pared ilusoria."FMe temo que Yezera y los otros se fueron. Solo somos tú… y yo."9Ganamos. No hay razón para que siga aquí. Ninguna."KAdemás del inmenso disfrute que extraeré al desmantelar a tu equipo."IUn amigo de Yezera. Aparte de eso, estoy enmascarado por una razón."aPreguntaría quién eres, pero siendo franco realmente no importa. Voy a descubrirlo pronto.":Sólo hay unos cuantos tipos de personas en el mundo."=Te lo acabo de decir: porque humillarte será divertido."VA no ser que te refieras a extraer a Regidrago, en cuyo caso, no, no te lo diré."kLos humanos tienen esta infuriante autodestructiva necesidad de contar secretos. Yo soy mejor que eso."3Bueno, veo que el diálogo no duró demasiado."Bien. Sufre."%Pero no vine aquí para charlar."rTe lo aseguro, no es nada personal – nadie ha tenido nada interesante que decir. Tú no eres la excepción."[Pero tu eres especialmente habilidoso, lo entiendo, y eso está correlacionado al ego.".Déjame mostrarte lo que realmente vales."p…Ah, que así sea. Dudo que pudiera infundir algo de humildad a tráves de tu dura cabeza de todos modos."CEres bueno jugando a los juegos superficiales – bien por ti.">Ibis, sácanos de aquí. Ya he visto más que suficiente."oSe escaparon. Ganaron. Algunos que estaban enmascarados, incluyendo quién demonios fuera ESO. Y Yezera…"_Ojalá supiera. Ese tipo era un narcisista y un idiota, eso es todo lo que te puedo decir."&El resto de ellos… quién sabe." Podría ser cualquier cosa."wPero si estaban buscando específicamente a Regidrago, y Yezera estaba con ellos… quizá incluso liderandolos…",…No lo sé. No tiene ningún sentido."IElla debería ser la última persona que llevaría a cabo algo así."PLo es. Ahora es tu problema, y sé que no te va a gustar eso, pero así es.":Esto es más grande que sólo un Pokémon legendario."/Te contaré un gran secreto abierto, ¿Ok?"~Las cuevas alrededor de Makya son tumbas para los Regis. Las extrañas de las que estaba hablando antes. Unas como estas."]Bueno, unos cuantos equipos arqueológicos fueron a estudiarlos hace un par de décadas."~E incluso encontraron a los Regis, unas ricas vetas de minerales, y las ruinas, y entendieron que podían aprovechar todo eso."�Conseguimos un poco de soporte corporativo de parte de Andris y Mavis, y boom: Team Chasm. Yo era uno de esos arqueologos originales."�…Algunos de nosotros. Helena quería estar al mando de su propia región. Andris quería una parte de todo ese crimen organizado."OY yo, estudiar a los Regis. Y algunas personas querían dejarme bien sola."mTenía un equipo con Regidrago a mi lado, y ellos no, así que podía estudiar lo que malditas quisiera."VAlgunos de nosotros. Yo no. Tenía cinco Regis – ¿Para qué necesitaba dinero?"MSi quería equipamiento de laboratorio, le mandaría una lista a Helena."\Vivía en una estación de investigación y comía ramen. Los mejores días de mi vida."qSólo quería estudiar a los Regis, y con su poder, nadie podía decirme que no. Gracioso como eso funciona."%Lo haces sonar tan puro y noble."vTenía curiosidad. Quería respuestas. Las obtuve – ¿Quién podría decirme que no con un Regidrago a mi lado?"\Por no mencionar el poderío del Team Chasm, porque mi investigación era MUY rentable."VEstaba llegando a eso, pero también, hey, podrías ser útil algún día, ¿Sí?"AComo estaba diciendo: encontramos a los cinco Regis menores."XMe tomó años, pero decifré sus inscripciones y entendí su verdadera naturaleza."eEso nos llevó a Regigigas, y a ese punto estabamos abarcando más de lo que podíamos sostener."[Gigas era más poderoso que el resto de los Regis juntos, y también más inteligente."{Moldear la tierra, revertirla a un tipo de arcilla primigenia. Crear sellos y guardias a los que nada podría atravesarlos."2Y, claro, podía usar un potente Gigaimpacto."jTambién podía hacer… otras cosas. Encontramos una manera de crear Pokémon etéreos con su poder."=Eran hostiles, poderosos – tenían que ser encerrados."�Y para el momento en el que Yezera pateó nuestra puerta y nos dijo que paremos, estaba básicamente confirmando lo que ya sabíamos."sEstabamos jugando con fuego. Si seguíamos usando a Regigigas, corríamos el real riesgo de destruir el mundo."qO al menos permanentemente cambiarlo. Así que pusimos a cada Regi de vuelta a su tumba y fuimos legítimos."kLas tumbas fueron reforzadas, por supuesto – nada puede atravesar las cámaras de los Regis menores."RLa cámara de Gigas sólo puede ser abierta por los otros cinco Regis juntos."\No lo sé. Ella estaba de acuerdo: era muy peligroso. Éramos criminales, no lunaticos."KSé que las cosas… no han ido bien con ella, ¿Pero esto? Es insano."iQuién sabe. Sabíamos que algunos grupos estaban intentando recuperarlos – siempre lo han estado."U¿Pero lograrlo? No había forma. Imposible. Pero… aparentemente Yezera puede."3…Probablemente. Puede que ya lo hayan hecho."dPero la cámara de Gigas está en lo profundo, y si no han roto el sello aún, sería por nada."[O si la han vuelto a sellar. Puedo intentar ir y comprobarlo, pero… no prometo nada."VMi PUNTO es que si no ayudas, mejor que te acostumbres a ver sólo piedra blanca.">Vas a ver mucho de eso si alguien deja libre a Regigigas."4Escucha, no lo sé. No sé un montón de cosas."�Así que déjame hablar con Andris, nuestros rangers, Helena, a quién sea que pueda encontrar. Ya veremos qué mal están las cosas."XY si esos ladrones muestran sus caras arriba del suelo, puedes enfrentarte a ellos."�Tienen por lo menos un Regi, probablemente más, así que hay una fuerte tentación para sembrar el caso. Creeme – lo sabría."HOdio decir esto, pero tienes que continuar siendo tú mismo, chico."DO, no, no debería llamarte chico. Toma esto – te lo ganaste."USolíamos darle estos a los equipos de asalto Chasm, para investigar las cuevas."UPodrás llegar a cualquier parte de la región – nadie se esconde de ti ahora."=Así que consigue esas medallas y salva el día, héroe."�Cambiar la dirección del compartimento estanco\nPuedes poner la llama en el palo superior para agarrar el inferior y llevarla contigo"aPrende la Vela que cuando recibe la llama proyecta una sombra en algún lado de la mazmorra."¿Quién eres?"¿Por qué haces esto?"Cállate, edgelord."¿Quién eres?"¿Qué es lo que quieren?"¿Por qué Yezera?"No es mi problema."¿Querías poder?"¿Querías dinero?"¿Querías conocimiento?"$¿Por qué debería importarme?" Entonces por qué Yezera…"'¿Cuántos Regis han sido robados?" Están abriendo esa puerta."¿Tu punto?;[e"*Multiple candles required for one fog"KJunction blocked by candle. Acts as a battery for flames between rooms"!Doesn't open from this side."^Airlock: Need to spend flame(s) in the top section to retrieve flame(s) in bottom section"Flame after illusory wall"PYezera and the others are gone, I’m afraid. It’s just you… and… me.":We won. No reason for me to be here. Absolutely none."XOther than the immense enjoyment I’m about to extract from dismantling your team."EA friend of Yezera’s. Besides that, I’m masked for a reason."iI would ask who you are, but quite frankly it doesn’t matter. I’m going to find out soon enough."9There’s only so many types of people in the world.":I just told you: because humiliating you will be fun."MUnless you mean extracting Regidrago, in which case, no, I won’t tell."bHumans have this infuriatingly self-destructive need to tell secrets. I’m better than that."3Well, I see the dialogue’s broken down fast."Fine. Suffer."6But I didn’t come here to engage in small talk."iI assure you, it isn’t personal – no one has anything interesting to say. You’re no exception."WBut you are exceptionally skilled, I understand, and that’s correlated with ego."5Allow me to show you what you’re really worth."V…Ah, so be it. I doubt I could drill humility through your thick skull anyways."=You’re good at playing shallow games – good for you."<Ibis, get us out of here. I’ve seen more than enough."hThey got away. They won. A few that were masked, including whoever the hell THAT was. And Yezera…"UWish I knew. That guy was a narcissist and an asshole, I can tell you that much."#The rest of them… who knows."Could be anything."jBut if they were after Regidrago specifically, and Yezera’s with them… maybe even leading them…"4…I don’t know. It doesn’t make any sense.">She should be the last person to pull this kind of stunt."XIt is. It’s your problem now, and I know you aren’t gonna like that, but it is."5This is bigger than just one legendary Pokémon."7I’m gonna let you in on the big open secret, OK?"oThe caves around Makya are tombs for the Regis. The weird ones I was talking about before. Ones like this."NWell, some archaeological teams went to study them a couple decades back."yAnd then they found the Regis, and the rich mineral veins, and the ruins, and they figured they could leverage that."{We got some corporate backing from Andris and Mavis, and boom: Team Chasm. I was one of those original archaeologists."n…Some of us. Helena wanted to run her own region. Andris wanted a piece of the organized crime bigtime."QMe, I study the Regis. And some people wanted me to leave well enough alone."jI had a Team and Regidrago on my side, and they didn’t, so I got to study what I damn well pleased."LSome of us. I didn’t. I had five Regis – what did I need money for?"8If I wanted lab equipment, I sent a list to Helena."GI lived in a research station and ate ramen. Best days of my life."oI just wanted to study the Regis, and with their power, nobody could tell me no. Funny how that works out.")You make it sound so pure and noble."bI was curious. Wanted answers. I got them – who could tell me no with Regidrago at my side?"YNot to mention the full might of Team Chasm, 'cause my research was VERY profitable."QI’m getting to that, but also, hey, it could come in handy some day, yeah?"5As I was saying: we found the five lesser Regis."\It took me years, but I deciphered their inscriptions and understood their true nature."JThat led us to Regigigas, and at that point we were cooking with gas."RGigas was stronger than the rest of the Regis put together, and smarter, too."|Shape the earth, revert it back to some kind of primordial clay. Create seals and wards that nothing could get through."2And, yeah, it could throw a mean Giga Impact."iIt could do… other things, too. We found a way to make it create ethereal Pokémon with its power.";They were hostile, powerful – had to be locked away."}And then by the time Yezera kicked down our door and told us to stop, she was basically just confirming what we already knew."pWe were playing with fire. If we kept using Regigigas, we ran the very real chance of destroying the world."`Or at least permanently changing it. So we put each Regi back in their tomb and went legit."iThe tombs were reinforced, of course – just about nothing can get through the minor Regi chambers."KGigas’s chamber can only be opened by the other five Regis together."_I don’t know. She agreed with us: it was too dangerous. We were criminals, not lunatics."MI know things… haven’t been great for her, but this? This is insane."[Who knows. We knew some groups were trying to get them back – they always have been."PBut succeeding? There was no way. Impossible. But… apparently Yezera can."*…Probably. They might already have."nGigas’s chamber is deep down, though, and if they haven’t broken the seal yet, it’d be for nothing."QOr if they’ve resealed it. I can try and scout it out, but… no promises."^My POINT is that if you don’t help out, you better get used to the look of white stone."]You’re gonna be seeing a whole lot more of it if someone tells Regigigas to let loose."<Listen, I don’t know. I don’t know a lot of things."sSo let me talk to Andris, our rangers, Helena, whoever else I can find. We’ll figure out how bad things are."PAnd if these thieves show their faces aboveground, you can brawl with them."~They’ve got at least one Regi, probably more, so there’s a strong temptation to wreak havoc. Trust me – I’d know."JHate to say it, but you just need to keep being your usual self, kid."JOr, no, I shouldn’t call you kid. Take this – you’ve earned it."AUsed to give these to Chasm strike teams, for cave scouting."UIt’ll get you just about anywhere in the region – nobody hides from you now."3So go get those badges and save the day, hero."jMisleading Airlock\nYou can put a flame in the upper stick to grab the lower one and take it with you"LLit Candle that when taking flame casts shadow somewhere in the dungeon"Who are you?"Why are you doing this?"Shut up, edgelord."Who are they?"What do they want?"Why Yezera?"Not my problem."You wanted power?"You wanted money?"You wanted knowledge?"Why should I care?"Then why is Yezera..."How many Regis are stolen?"They're opening that door."Your point?Iu;␀�-[[]"	\PN."gY’know, I pretty much assumed this was going to be a trap, but I didn’t think you’d be here.",Well... whatcha doing? Care to explain?"7What? You want me to explain this? Velenz? *shrug*">Oh, I know. But you’re the one standing in front of me."LCute. Never should’ve brought a hero here. Heroes are always trouble.")*snort* Sure, kid. Whatever you say."vI know you’re here with that girl – Candy? Helena’s had her trackers keeping an eye on her for a while now."JShe hasn’t been causing too much trouble, though, so we let her go."dListen, we ran this region. Do you know what that means – taken any political science lately?"JIt means a monopoly on violence. Every government works the same way."BOh, you can call me a tyrant if you want, but I’m no thief."Yep! And a damn good one."fNot an absolute one, though – Andris and Helena made up the other two corners of that triangle."JNot to mention the extensive bureaucracy of Team Chasm at its height."@From who? This was a lawless frontier before we came along."VOnly holdouts like Novo truly resisted unification into the larger establishment."hThe benefits of being a tyrant. If people are getting in the way, you can convince them to... stop."/C’mon. You were raised better than that."8We still rule the region because we ARE the region."�We’ve got old grunts everywhere who’ll still follow orders if I give them. Helena has her trackers, so we’ve got an intelligence agency."dAnd she’s got her claws in LuxTech’s outpost here, so economic development is guided by us."XWe were a big organization. All-encompassing. And we had to be: lots of work to do."uOver just a few decades, we imposed law on this place, created entire new settlements, made it rich and vibrant."�We quintupled the population. We dealt with outbreaks, infighting, earthquakes. We secured the support of multiple major companies."~And at the end of the day, we managed to go legit, integrate with the Prizcan government, and aren’t even hated for it."_If you want to try and do even a tenth of that without resorting to violence, be my guest."�We punished people, which you’d call assault. We imprisoned them, which you’d call kidnapping. We taxed them, which you’d call theft."FOh, sure, people resisted us, but we only acted how a state does."ECandy’s too young to have been around during Chasm’s zenith."~She’s got a child’s notion of justice, and she thinks that performing her own little acts of violence fixes anything."GMaybe she should ask herself why almost everyone’s fine with us."	Yes."Andris did it for money."Helena did it for power."WAnd I did it so I could finally have the resources to properly research the Regis."ZEveryone in Team Chasm – in any organization – has their own reasons to be there."F...We can argue all day, kid. You’re not going to get anywhere."Let me put it this way:"�a lot of the Pokémon Candy has “rescued” were given to Chasm grunts for combat purposes, but they ended up liking their new home plenty fine."PMaybe talking things out would’ve resolved things better than theft, huh?"gBut I know you want to know. What’s up with Velenz? Well, it’s simple. We were trying to work."�I can’t work when I’m being attacked by wannabe heroes. When the power grid is being fried. When Ghost-types are being sent to haunt my lab.";We asked, repeatedly, for them to stop. They didn’t."tSo I took Regigigas and had it carve up the bedrock around here, then dragged some avatars in for good measure."zThey couldn’t prove it was us, but pretty soon they lost their base of operations, and that got the message across."LYes. Was. If they’d wanted to keep it, they could’ve left us alone."?Kid, have you ever gotten twelve hours of sleep in a week?"vThese “freedom fighters” were using every trick in the book. Constantly harrying us. Never a moment’s rest.".Ugh. Makes me mad just thinking about it."I think so, yeah."NThat’s how it goes. Warfare ain’t pretty, but it exists for a reason."qI did what I did. And if someone wants to “bring me to justice” for it, I say: what does that even mean?"LI’m breaking my back running this region, making it better every day."fYou want to throw me in prison? Make this place worse so you can have your petty revenge? Idiocy."SI know what I did, and I’m not going to do it again. Neither is anyone else."|...Now, kid. I need to get out of this place, because I don’t particularly want to run into Candy. Get out of my way."NYou need to work on your active listening. I didn’t ask you a question."MI told you what you were going to do… and now you’re going to do it."Ugh. Heroes!"3Damn heroes... well, what’d I really expect."Get up."CI’m not angry, just disappointed. But I will be taking my–"\PN! Tamarind!"xStop right there. I – I know I took, um, a little bit to get here, but that’s only because I was eavesdropping!";Candy, is it? Good to meet you in person... I suppose."5You know where I stand. And I know where you do."�I’ve just settled things with \PN, so why don’t we have a chat in private? \PN, be a dear for me and leave us. I’d like to end this grudge here and now."Z...Alright. This is between you and me, anyways. \PN, you can go, like, wait outside."+Just for a minute. This’ll be quick.".Good. Glad we can see eye to eye on this."You first."Not my idea."Getting answers."Delivering justice."Tyrant."You seized power."And Velenz?"You don't rule anymore."Not just violence."Some hate you."You did it for yourself."It was their home."That seems excessive."Fair enough."..."No."...Alright.[]"	\PN."aSabes, había asumido que esto iba a ser una trampa, pero no pensé que tú estarías aquí."4Bueno... ¿Qué haces? ¿Te importa explicarme?">¿Qué? ¿Quiéres que explique esto? ¿Velenz? Como sea.";Oh, lo sé. Pero tú eres quien está en frente de mi."fAdorable. Nunca debería haber traído a un héroe aquí. Los héroes son siempre problemáticos."+*resoplo* Seguro, chico. Lo que digas."gSé que estás aquí con esa chica – ¿Candy? Helena la tiene rastreada desde hace un tiempo ya."CAunque no ha causado muchos problemas, así que la dejamos ir."sEscucha, dirigimos esta región. ¿Sabes lo que eso significa – has tomado ciencias políticas últimamente?"^Eso significa un monopolio en violencia. Todos los gobiernos funcionan de la misma forma."HOh, puedes llamarme una tirana si quieres, pero no soy una ladrona."/¡Sip! Y puedes apostar que era una buena."iPero no una absoluta – Andris y Helena formaban parte de las otras dos esquinas de ese triángulo."FPor no mencionar la extensa burocracia del Team Chasm en su pico."K¿De quién? Esta era una frontera sin leyes antes de que llegáramos."jSólo pocas resistencias como Novo realmente resistieron la unificación en un establecimiento mayor."eBeneficios de ser una tirana. Si la gente se pone en tu camino, puedes convencerlos de... parar.")Vamos. Fuiste criador mejor que eso."=Todavía mandamos en la región porque SOMOS la región."�Tenemos antiguos reclutas en toda la región que todavía seguirían órdenes si se las diéramos. Helena tiene sus rastreadores, así que tenemos una agencia de inteligencia."~Y ella tiene sus garras en la división de LuxTech aquí, así que el desarrollo de la economía es guíado por nosotros."sEramos una gran organización. Abarcábamos todo. Y teníamos que hacerlo: había demasiado trabajo que hacer."{Durante sólo un par de décadas, impusimos la ley en este lugar, creamos nuevos asentamientos, lo hicimos rico y vibrante."�Quintuplicamos la población. Nos encargamos de brotes, disputas internas, terremotos. Nos aseguramos el apoyo de múltiples grandes compañías."|Al final del día, pudimos salir legítimos, nos integramos con el gobierno de Prizca, y ni siquiera nos odian por eso."_Si quieres intentar y hacer una décima de eso sin recurrir a la violencia, déjame verlo."�Castigábamos a la gente, lo que llamarías asalto. Los encerrábamos, lo que llamarías secuestro. Les hacíamos pagar impuestos, lo que llamarías robo."UOh, seguro, la gente se nos resistía, sólo actuábamos como un estado lo hace."LCandy es demasiado jóven para haber estado durante el cénit de Chasm."uTiene un sentido de la justicia infantil, y ella piensa que hacer sus pequeños actos de violencia arregla algo."OQuizás debería preguntarse por qué casi todos están bien con nosotros."	Sí."Andris lo hizo por dinero."Helena lo hizo por poder."jY yo lo hice así finalmente podríamos tener los recursos para investigar adecuadamente a los Regis."kTodos en el Team Chasm – en cualquier organización – tenía sus propios motivos para estar allí."N...Podemos discutir todo el día, chico. No vas a llegar a ninguna parte.""Déjame ponerlo de este modo:"�Muchos de los Pokémon que Candy "rescató" fueron dados a los reclutas Chasm por motivos de combate, pero terminaron gustando su nuevo hogar sin mayor problema."ZQuizás hablar las cosas habría resuelto las cosas de mejor forma que el robo, ¿Eh?"hPero sé lo que quieres saber. ¿Qué ocurre con Velenz? Bueno, es simple. Intentábamos trabajar,."�No puedo trabajar cuando estoy siendo atacada por supuestos héroes. Cuando la red eléctrica está siendo quemada. Cuando tipos Fantasmas son enviados a mi laboratorio."=Les pedimos, repetidamente, que pararan. No lo hicieron."Así que tomé a Regigigas e hice que partiera los cimientos alrededor, y luego trajé unos cuantos avatares por si acaso."vNo pudieron demostrar que fuimos nosotros, pero pronto perdieron su base de operaciones, y eso les hizo entender."FSí. Era. Si querían mantenerlo, podrían habernos dejado solos.">Niño, ¿Alguna vez has dormido doce horas en una semana?"}Estos "justicieros" estaban usando todos los trucos. Constantemente hostigándonos. Nunca con un momento para descansar."3Ugh. Me pone de los nervios sólo de pensarlo."Eso creo, sí."NAsí es como funciona. La guerra no es bonita, pero existe por un motivo."rHice lo que hice. Y si alguien quiere "llevarme a la justicia" por ello, digo: ¿Qué significa eso siquiera?"IMe rompo la espalda dirigiendo esta región, mejorándola cada día."r¿Quieres llevarme a prisión? ¿Hacer este lugar peor sólo para tener tu pequeña venganza? Es una idiotez."KSé lo que hice, y no lo voy a hacer de nuevo. Nadie más lo va hacer."~...Ahora, chico, tengo que salir de este lugar, porque no quiero particularmente encontrarme con Candy. Sal de mi camino."GTienes que trabajar en tu escucha activa. No te hice una pregunta."8Te dije lo que ibas hacer... y ahora vas a hacerlo."Ugh. ¡Héroes!"1Malditos héroes.. bueno, que más esperaba."Levántate."CNo estoy enojada, sólo decepcionado. Pero ahora voy a reti–"¡\PN! ¡Tamarind!"}No se muevan. Sé – sé que me tomé, em, lo suyo para llegar aquí, ¡Pero eso es sólo porque quería escuchar todo!"D¿Candy, me equivoco? Es bueno conocerte en persona... supongo."5Sabes cual es mi postura. Y sé cual es la tuya."�Acabo de resolver las cosas con \PN, ¿Así por qué no hablamos en privado? \PN, pórtate bien y déjanos. Quiero terminar este rencor aquí y ahora."[...Muy bien. Esto es entre tú y yo, de todos modos. \PN, puedes, ya sabes, ir afuera."-Sólo por un minuto. Esto será rápido."9Bien. Me agrada que nos pongamos de acuerdo en esto."Tú primero."No fue mi idea."Obteniendo respuestas."Repartiendo justicia."Tirana."Aprovechaste el poder."¿Y Velenz?"Ya no mandas."No sólo violencia."Algunos te odian."Lo hiciste por ti misma."Era su hogar."Eso parece excesivo."Es justo."..."No."...Muy bien.;[]"	\PN."gY’k