me."JThe most important thing to learn in your life is how to be generous."JI once gave $1,000,000 towards that Pokemon sanctuary west of Velenz."FJust talking about it's got me in a giving mood. Here, take this."KNow now, you wouldn't be asking me to give you another one, would you?"ZThe most important thing to learn in your life is how to be happy with what you have."Welcome, \PN!"*Oh, I can see the shock on your face."9I recognize you from pictures your mother showed me."PWe meet often at LuxTech events. She's a real business leader, your mother!"LI think it's fair for me to say that she's an inspiration to all of us."4I hope you enjoy yourself at our little soiree."NTrainers should just learn to surf with their Pokemon, like they used to."0Me and my Feraligatr were quite the pair..."LNasty business, that thing with the bridge. Good thing I have a boat..."SThis piece was sculpted by Noel, the Gym Leader on the eastern half of Prizca."&I can tell just by looking at it!"[You know, I had a keen interest in Noel even before all that nonsense with Team Chasm."*I've really hit my stride at LuxTech."IMoving smart and talking fast. Striking deals and meeting deadlines."0I could never show off my talents in Chasm."AThe nerve they had to assign me to the docks, of all places."LHere you are, a specialty of the Kalos Region, made fresh this morning!">My deepest apologies, it seems we've run out of Galettes."HJust talking about it has got me in a giving mood. Here, take this."2What in the world is wrong with this thing..."[You see the scientist struggle with a computer that is rapidly blinking and turns off."WThere's something up with this computer. If only I had a Porygon to work it out..."6Actually hey, could you go and get me one please?"�I've been needing one anyways, since I work with computers. So please do a trade with me for it, I'll figure out what to get you for it."iWell no rush, maybe it'll mysteriously start working again... and yes, I turned it off and on again.">Ah, alright. Check again with me if you change your mind."$Thank you, let's get it traded."nYou trade over the Porygon. It enters the computer, and a buzzing sound is heard as a Shedinja flies out."?You catch it to prevent it from causing any other trouble."{What the- it was actually a bug in there? Well damn, okay. You can keep it I guess, the computer is working perfectly."Thank you for this!"Yes[0"*Es difícil que yo pueda entrar ahí."dSólo me invitaron como una recompensa en las líneas de código escritas en el último cuarto."I¿Es eso siquiera una buena métrica de productividad? No lo creo…"G¿No te parece peculiar que esta casa es completamente simétrica?"2Y esa mezcla de estética de Kanto y Kalos…"<Quizás no estés de acuerdo, pero lo veo un tanto feo."OLa lección más importante que aprender en la vida es cómo ser generoso."JUna vez le dí $1.000.000 a un santuario Pokémon al oeste de Velenz."BSólo hablar de eso ya me puso de buen humor. Ven, toma esto."9Ahora, no me estarás pidiendo que te de otra, ¿No?"^La lección más importante que aprender en la vida es cómo ser feliz con lo que tienes."¡Bienvenido, \PN!"*Oh, puedo ver que estás sorprendido."9Te reconozco por unas fotos que tu madre me mostró."^Nos juntamos seguido en eventos de LuxTech. ¡Tu madre sí que es una líder de negocios!"NCreo que es justo decir que ella es una inspiración para todos nosotros."2Espero que disfrutes nuestra pequeña velada."MLos Entrenadores deberían volver a aprender a surfear con sus Pokémon.".Mi Feraligatr y yo éramos un gran par…"MVaya fastidio, esa cosa con el puente. Buena suerte que tengo un bote…"YEsta pieza fue esculpida por Noel, el líde rde gimnasio de la mitad este de Prizca."'¡Puedo decirlo con sólo mirarla!"`Sabes, tenía un gran interés en Noel incluso antes de todo ese sinsentido del Team Chasm.")Realmente tomé el ritmo en LuxTech."cMoverse de forma inteligente y hablar rápido. Hacer acuerdos y cumplir las fechas de entrega."2Nunca pude alardear de mis talentos en C