ack to cause double the damage taken."iThe target is crushed with great force. The attack is more powerful the more HP the target has left."JAn attack move that cuts down the target's HP to equal the user's HP."bThe user flails about aimlessly to attack. It becomes more powerful the less HP the user has."bThe user throws an exploding package at enemies, or one filled with healing treats at allies."KThe user shouts with force at the target. This move always hits first."yThe power stored using the move Stockpile is released all at once in an attack. 150 base power per Stockpile charge."dThe user chomps hard on the target with its sharp front fangs. It cuts the target's HP to half."eThe user unleashes its ultimate move. Can't miss and skips protections. Only one use per battle."bThe user powerfully wrings the foe. The more HP the foe has, the greater this attack's power."NThe user helps the target and makes it use its move right after the user."bThe user hurriedly and randomly uses a move among those known by other Pokémon in the party."vThe user switches places with a party Pokémon in waiting, passing along any stat step changes. Always goes last."TThe user maximizes its Attack stat in exchange for HP equal to half its max HP."WThe user passes its held item to the target when the target isn't holding an item."NThe user blocks the target's way with arms spread wide to prevent escape."`The user tells the target a secret, lowering its Sp. Atk by three steps. Always goes first."KThe user changes its type to become the same type as one of its moves."iThe user changes its type to make itself resistant to the type of the attack the opponent used last."lThe user mimics the move used immediately before it. The move fails if no other move has been used yet."TFor four turns, this move prevents the target from using the move it last used."ZThe user compels the target to keep using only the move it last used for three turns."aThe user endures any attack with at least 1 HP. It always fails if it is used in succession."jThe user dances to compel the target to mimic it, making the target's Ability the same as the user's."RThe user focuses intensely on the fight, quadrupling its critical hit chance."VThe user draws attention to itself, making all targets take aim only at the user."GThe user intimidates the target by staring at it to cause numbing."PThe user growls, scaring nearby foes. Their Attack is lowered by two steps."_The user's body grows all at once, raising Atk and Sp. Atk by two steps, or 4 in sunshine."\The user stiffens all the muscles in its body to raise its Defense stat by three steps."`The user makes a soothing bell chime to heal the status problems of all the party Pokémon."NThe user assists an ally by boosting the power of its next attack by 50%."VThe user howls loudly to raise its Attack by three steps, and its allies' by one."^The user focuses intensely. The attack on the next turn always results in a critical hit."_The user leers at nearby foes with sharp eyes. Their Defense stat is reduced by two steps."`The user chants an incantation, preventing the foe from landing critical hits for 10 turns."hThe user tries to cut ahead of the foe to steal and use the foe's intended move with greater power."]The user pins the target with a dark, arresting look. The target becomes unable to flee."\The user waggles a finger and stimulates its brain into randomly using nearly any move."hThe user copies the move last used by the foe. The move can be used until the user is switched out."fAn attack that makes use of nature's power. Its effects vary depending on the user's environment."ZThe user intimidates all nearby foes, lowering their Attack and Sp. Atk by two steps."bThe user adds its HP to the target's HP, then equally shares the combined HP with the target."_Any Pokémon that hears this song faints in three turns, unless it switches out of battle."NIt enables the user to evade all attacks. It fails if used in succession."PThe user hypnotizes itself into copying any stat change made by the target."QRestoring its own cells, the user restores its own HP by half of its max HP."XThe user recycles a held item that has been used in battle so it can be used again."PThe user reflects the target's type, making it the same type as the target.";The user rests to cure itself of any status condition."[The foe is forced to switch out to a random ally. Always goes last. Ends wild battles."UThe user creates a protective field that prevents status problems for ten turns."\The user frightens the target with a scary face to reduce its Speed stat by four steps."UThe user's earsplitting screech reduces the target's Defense stat by four steps."KThe user edges become sharper, raising its Attack stat by three steps."~The user breaks its shell, lowering its Defense and Sp. Def by two steps but raising attacking and Speed stats by three steps."SThe user shoots a mysterious beam that changes the target's Ability to Simple."\A soothing lullaby is sung in a calming voice that puts the target into a deep slumber."jIt enables the user to permanently learn the move last used by the foe. Once used, Sketch disappears."OThe user slacks off, restoring its own HP by up to half of its maximum HP."JWhile it is asleep, the user randomly uses one of the moves it knows."BThe user restores its own HP by up to half of its maximum HP."CThe user just flops and splashes around to no effect at all..."`The user shines a spotlight on the target so that only it will be attacked during the turn."cThe user charges up power and raises both its Defense and Sp. Def. The move can be used twice."rThe user spends 25% HP to create a doll to protect it from move damage, additional affects, and status moves."PThe user generates odd sound waves from its body. The target becomes dizzy."|The power stored using the move Stockpile is absorbed by the user to heal its HP. 50% max HP heal per Stockpile charge."dA frenetic dance to uplift the fighting spirit. It raises the user's Attack stat by four steps."^The user gets teary eyed. This lowers the target's Attack and Sp. Atk stats by two steps."JThe user performs a wobbly dance that dizzies the Pokémon around it."]The user tickles the target into laughing, reducing its Attack and Defense by two steps."ZThe user transforms into a copy of the target right down to having the same move set."aOne turn after this move is used, the target's HP is restored by half the user's maximum HP."EThe user is roused, raising its Attack and Sp. Atk by two steps."WThe user yawns, making the target drowsy. They'll fall asleep at end of turn next."WWith its mysterious power, the user swaps the effects on either side of the field."XThe user eats its held Berry, then  raises both its defensive stats by three steps."aThe user has teatime with all the Pokémon in the battle. Each Pokémon eats its held Berry."gThe user lets out a damaging belch at the target. The user must eat a held Berry to use this move."[The user shoots filthy garbage at the target to attack. It has a 10% chance to poison."`It swamps the area around the user with a giant sludge wave. It has a 10% chance to poison."dThe target is stabbed with a tentacle or arm seeped with poison. It has a 10% chance to poison."gA slashing attack with a poisonous blade that has a 20% chance to poison. Can random critical hit."NUnsanitary sludge is hurled at the target. It has a 30% chance to poison."jThe user drenches the foe in a special poisonous liquid. Its power doubles if the target is poisoned."pThe user attacks with a cloud of white smoke. All of the target's stat step changes are returned to normal."LThe user bites the target with toxic fangs with a 50% chance to poison."EThe user hits the target with its tail. Can random critical hit."ZThe foe is attacked with a spray of harsh acid. It has a 20% chance to lower Sp. Def."nThe user spits fluid that works to melt the target. This reduces the target's Sp. Def stat by four steps."\The target is attacked with a discharge of filthy gases. It has a 30% chance to poison."YThe user stabs the target with a poisonous stinger. This has a 30% chance to poison."iThe user coils up and concentrates. This raises its Attack, Defense, and Accuracy by two steps each."]A cloud of poison gas is sprayed in the face of opposing Pokémon. It poisons those hit."]The user heals the target's status condition. If so, it also restores the user's own HP."jThe user shoots poisonous threads to poison the target and lowers the target's Speed stat by 4 steps."WNearby poisoned foes have their Attack, Sp. Atk, and Speed lowered by three steps."lInflicts physical or special damage, whichever will be more effective. This has a 25% chance to poison."fThe user shoots powerful lasers using the power of a prism. The user can't move on the next turn."TTwo turns after this move is used, a hunk of psychic energy attacks the target."YUsing an odd shock wave, the user damages any Pokémon of the same type as the user."UHeals the user for 50% of the damage caused. Power doubles if the foe is asleep."NThe user attacks with a pillar of dark light. This ignores their ability."[The target is hit by a strong telekinetic force. It has a 20% chance to lower Sp. Def."pThe user bites the target using psychic capabilities. Also breaks any screens protecting the target's side."bThe user attacks with an odd, unseeable power. It has a 40% chance to make the target flinch."�Using a hyperspace hole, the user appears right next to the target and strikes. Skips and destroys protections and substitutes. Always hits."fThe user materializes an odd psychic wave to attack the target. This attack does physical damage."sThe user focuses its willpower to its head and attacks the foe. It has a 40% chance to make the target flinch."eThe user lets loose a damaging burst of light. It also lowers the target's Sp. Def by two steps."qA mistlike flurry of down envelops and damages the target. It also lowers the target's Sp. Atk by two steps."_The user tears at the target with blades formed by psychic power. Can random critical hit."NThe target is attacked with a peculiar ray. It has a 10% chance to dizzy."`The user unleashes a vicious blow after a cute act. It has a 50% chance to cause flinching."QThe target is hit by a weak telekinetic force. It has a 10% chance to dizzy."fThe user attacks with stored power. The more the user's stats are raised, the greater the damage."]A retaliation move that counters any special attack, inflicting double the damage taken."UThe target is attacked with an odd psychic wave. The attack varies in intensity."\The user relaxes and lightens its body to move faster, raising its Speed by four steps."\The user teleports using a strange power and switches its place with one of its allies."nThe user temporarily empties its mind to forget its concerns. It raises the user's Sp. Def by four steps."UThe user quietly focuses its mind to raise its Sp. Atk and Sp. Def by two steps."`The user absorbs a mystical power from space to raise its Defense and Sp. Def by two steps."mGravity is intensified for five turns, forcing Pokemon down from the air and doubling all move accuracy."pThe user employs psychic power to average its base Defense and base Sp. Def stats with those of its target."iFor five turns, the foe is prevented from using any moves, Abilities, or held items that recover HP."_The user emits a healing pulse which restores the target's HP by up to half of its max HP."jThe user faints. In return, the Pokémon taking its place will have its HP restored and status cured."TThe user employs its psychic power to switch stat step changes with the target."GThe user instructs the target to use the target's last move again."_A wondrous wall of light is put up to suppress damage from special attacks for five turns."_Until end of turn, reflects status moves that target the user or create hazards around it."oThe user employs psychic power to average its base Attack and base Sp. Atk stats with those of the target."YThe user employs psychic power to switch its base Attack with its base Defense stat."aUsing its psychic power of suggestion, the user transfers its status problems to the target."`A wondrous wall of light is put up to suppress damage from physical attacks for five turns."UThe user goes to sleep to fully restore their HP and heal any status conditions."QThe user mimics the target completely, copying the target's natural Ability."NThe user employs its psychic power to exchange Abilities with the target."LThe user switches out to a party Pokémon in waiting. Always goes last."PThe user catches the target off guard and swaps its held item with its own."_The user creates a bizarre area in which slower Pokémon get to move first for five turns."bThe user casts a horrible spell on the opponent. This removes 4 PP from their last used move."aThe user shoots its psychic power from its eyes to attack. It has a 20% chance to frostbite."dThe user attacks the foe with a hazardous, full-power headbutt. The user also takes 50% recoil."fThe user launches a huge boulder at the target to attack. It must rest on the next turn, however."[The user whips up a storm of diamonds to damage foes, raising its Defense and Sp. Def."VThe user stabs the foe with sharpened stones from below. Can random critical hit."XThe user attacks with a ray of light that sparkles as if it were made of gemstones."eLarge boulders are hurled at the foes to inflict damage. It has a 30% chance to cause flinching."WThe user attacks with a prehistoric power. It has a 20% chance to raise all stats."WBoulders are hurled at the target. It also lowers the target's Speed by two steps."GThe user picks up and throws a small rock at the target to attack."iThe user throws a stone or projectile to attack. A flying Pokémon will fall to the ground when hit."QThe user smashes into the target at high speed. This move always goes first."aThe user hurls hard rocks at the target. Two to five rocks are launched 