t switch into battle. It deals double damage in rainstorm."VTurns the foe's power against it, dealing damage using the target's Sp. Atk stat."FThe user fires a dimensional mote, lowering the target's Sp. Def."MBy sacrificing half its total HP, the user makes the target fall asleep."qDoubles in power if the foe is asleep. The user's HP is restored by 50% the damage dealt. This can overheal."dSummons eclipse for eight turns, boosting Psychic-type attacks and heralding the total eclipse."lThe target's psyche is attacked directly. It has a 30% chance to lower the target's Attack and Sp. Atk."fThe target is hit by a weak telekinetic force. It has a 10% chance to lower the target's Sp. Def."nThe user covers the field with an fog of ice crystals, summoning hail and creating Grey Mist for 5 turns."rThe user makes the target to trip into a huge pile of snow, damaging them and summoning hail for eight turns."XDrains the heat from the target. The user's HP is restored by 50% the damage dealt."rProtects the user from attacks. If an eclipse is active, extends it by one turn. Fails if used in succession."`The user whips up a tornado to tear at the target. It has a 30% chance to make them flinch."�The user insults the target using a compliment. The target's attacking stats are raised by 3 steps, but they hurt themselves in confusion."`The user disarms the target's blade. The target cannot use blade-based moves for two turns."GThe target is forced underwater for a brief time, waterlogging it."XThe user pushes the target violently into water. This has a 10% chance to waterlog."PFor the rest of the round, the healing of all damaged Pokémon is reversed."VThe target is dragged viciously through water. This has a 30% chance to waterlog."hThe user chomps hard, cutting the target's HP by 50%, and the user's HP is restored by 50% of that."oThe user submerges the target in water, then bludgeons them repeatedly. This has a 10% chance to waterlog."]The target is pranked with a huge bucket of water. This has a 50% chance to waterlog it."JAn enchanting outcry. This attack never misses and skips protections."TThe user makes a fool out of the target. This has a 50% chance of jinxing them."aThe user plays with the target with unneccessary force. It has a 50% chance to lower Attack."fThe user hopes for bad luck, jinxing the target. Attacks against them crit and pierce protection."]The user causes an accident, damaging the target. This has a 30% chance of jinxing them."XThe user causes the target to trip and fall. This has a 50% chance of jinxing them."cThe user causes nearby objects to fall onto the target. This has a 30% chance of jinxing them."JThe user invokes the target's true name as a fae curse, jinxing them."bA spray of bubbles is forcefully ejected at all nearby foes, lowering their Speed by 3 steps."NThe user inflicts waterlog on all nearby foes. User becomes a Water-type."`The user draws attention to itself, making all targets take aim only at the user this turn."dThe user sticks out its head and attacks by charging into the foe. It has a 50% chance to numb."HThe foe is forced to switch out to a random ally. Always goes last.";An attack that can be used only if the user is asleep."oA barrage of two to five star-shaped rays are shot at the opposing team. Can't miss and skips protections."=Used only if the user has no PP. It also hurts the user."ZThe user consumes its Stockpile to heal for 50% max HP per charge. This can overheal."_The user cleans the target aggressively with soapy water. It has a 50% chance to waterlog."XThe user spins the target with a cleansing vortex. It has a 30% chance to waterlog."_The target is struck by a pulse of negative energy. This resets the target's stat changes."lThe user shoots out a quick flash of bioluminescence to damage the target. This move always goes first."_The user attacks with small beams of light. It has a 20% chance to make the target flinch."mThe user attacks with a blinding flash of bioluminscence. It has a 40% chance to make the target flinch."vThe user sheds a huge volley of scales at the target. Lands without fail and lowers the user's Sp. Def and Speed."pThe user opens its soul to unleash massive energy. This lowers the user's Sp. Atk and Sp. Def by two steps."dThe user headbutts the target with a metal head. It has a 20% chance to make the target flinch."hThe user conserves for future attacks. This raises its Sp. Atk, Sp. Def, and Accuracy by two steps."}The user creates a storm using its flaming body, damaging everything around it and melting away hazards from both sides."XThe user creates an electric fueled cage, trapping and damaging it for three turns."yThe user psychically exploits weak points in the target's mind. Can random critical hit, and does so twice as often."OThe target is scrutinized, damaging their psyche. Can random critical hit."eThe user takes control of the target's mind to unleash an attack on it. Can random critical hit."ZThis attack deals 50% more damage if the target has any raised or lowered stat steps."tThe user smacks the target and steals its item while it is stunned. Items stolen from wild Pokémon are stored."=The user copies and gains the first ability of each foe."�A move that only the avatar of Groudon can use. For the rest of the battle, gravity is intensified and Pokemon have their weight doubled."WEnables random critical hits for the user, and quadruples its critical hit chance."GA slashing attack with a poisonous blade. Can random critical hit."AThe user launches a fiery kick. It has a 10% chance to burn."QThe target is struck with a supersonic water blast. Can random critical hit."RThe target is blasted with a forceful shot of water. Can random critical hit."jThe user hits the target with throwing stars two to five times in a row. This move always goes first."vEnables random critical hits for the user, quadruples its critical hit chance, and raises its Speed by two steps."aThe user suffocates the target by sucking the air from their lungs. Can random critical hit."aThe user thins the air around the target, depriving them of oxygen. Can random critical hit."LThe target is pierced with a sharp iron arrow. Can random critical hit."QThe target is pierced with a pointed metal javelin. Can random critical hit."tThe user shoots a massive metal object at the target. The user must rest on the next turn to regain its energy."[The user launches a concentrated ball of searing white flame. Can random critical hit."gLays roots that heal the user by absorbing 1/8th HP from foes each turn. The user becomes trapped."�The user and the target pit their energy against one another. The damage is based on the target's Sp. Atk rather than their Sp. Def."ZThe user breaks down all insulation to send a barrage of electricity for three turns."KThe user dizzies the target, then welcomes in eclipse for eight turns."iThe user psychically alters the target's brain to forget. This move disables the target's last move."lThe target is put to sleep via a deep freeze. The user must rest on the next turn to regain its energy."�The user insults the target using a compliment. Their Attack and Sp. Atk are raised by three steps, but they hurt themselves in confusion."QThe target's mind is overloaded with emotion. Applies Torment to the target."gThe user shoots a magical arrow which seeks out the target's weak points. Can random critical hit."LThe user leeches the target, then welcomes in moonglow for eight turns."VThe user blasts the target with highly pressurized sand. Can random critical hit."ZThe user rocks out by using each Sound-based move they know. Only one use per battle."cThe user breaks down all insulation to send a barrage of electricity to rampage for two turns."fDamages all near foes by summoning a miniature black hole. Gravity is intensified for five turns."cThe user sets Grey Mist for 8 turns, gives themselves a Black Sludge, and becomes Poison-type.">The user restores its own HP by up to half of its max H