 that crawls along the ground. Those it hits can't flee from battle."7The user burrows, then attacks on the second turn."dThe user crashes into its target while rotating its body like a drill. Can random critical hit."UThe user attacks driven by frustration. Power increases if previous move failed."ZThe user clubs the target with a bone. It has a 50% chance to make the target flinch."fThe user strikes everything around it by stomping on the ground. It reduces hit Pokémon's Speed."oThe user attacks by shooting a beam of mud at the target. It also reduces the target's Speed by two steps."aThe user throws the bone it holds. The bone loops to hit the target twice, coming and going."\The user spins a sandstorm around the target, trapping and damaging it for three turns."MThe user strikes the target with a hard bone two to five times in a row."`The user looses a ground-shaking quake affecting everyone around. Its power varies greatly."OThe user regains up to half of its max HP. It restores 66% in a sandstorm."hThe user lays spikes at the foe's feet. Foes that switch into battle are hurt a bit for each layer."PThrows scorching sand at the target to attack. It has a 10% chance to burn."jOn the second turn, the user hits the foe with electrically charged ice. It has a 30% chance to numb."dOn the second turn, an ultracold, freezing wind surrounds the foe. It has a 30% chance to burn."SA blizzard strikes all near foes. Can't miss in hail. 30% chance to frostbite."`The user swings and hits with its strong, heavy fist. Lowers the user's Speed by two steps."\The target is struck with an icy-cold beam of energy. It has a 10% chance to frostbite."pThe user attacks by harshly dropping an icicle onto the foe. It has a 30% chance to make the target flinch."NThe target is punched with an icy fist. It has a 10% chance to frostbite."XThe target is hit with a rainbow-colored beam. It has a 30% chance to lower Attack."yThe user attacks by blowing freezing cold air at all near foes. This attack reduces the targets' Speed by two steps."iThe user bites with cold-infused fangs. It has a 10% chance to flinch and a 10% chance to frostbite."^The user blows a cold breath on the target. This attack always results in a critical hit."fThe user attacks with a gust of chilled air. It also lowers the targets' Speed stat by two steps."dThe user flash freezes chunks of ice and hurls them at the target. This move always goes first."]The user attacks with a chilling gust of powdery snow. It has a 10% chance to frostbite."PThe user rolls into the target. Its power doubles if it hits in succession."ZThe user launches sharp icicles at the target. It strikes two to five times in a row."`This move reduces damage from attacks for five turns. This can be used only in a hailstorm."MSummons hail for six turns. Damages non-Ice, non-Ghost-types every turn."YA consecutive three-kick attack that becomes more powerful with each successful hit."VThe user attacks by hurling a blizzard-cloaked icicle lance at opposing Pokémon."bThe user explodes to inflict damage on those around it. The user faints upon using this move."fThe user charges at the target using every bit of its power. The user must rest on the next turn."hThe foe is attacked with a powerful beam. The user must rest on the next turn to regain its energy."eThe user attacks everything around it with the destructive power of a terrible, explosive sound."cThis move can be used only after the user has used all the other moves it knows in the battle."mThe user tucks in to raise its Defense by four steps in the first turn, then rams the foe on the second."EA reckless, life-risking tackle. The user also takes 33% recoil."_The user charges its head into the foe. As a result, it takes 2/3 of the damage as recoil."jThe user fires a beam of light at its target. The type changes depending on the Drive the user holds."NA large egg is hurled at the target with maximum force to inflict damage."lThe user releases countless shots of light. Its type varies with the kind of Plate the user is holding."SThe user lets loose a horribly echoing shout with the power to inflict damage."qCloaking itself in high energy, the user slams into the target. This move's type depends on the held memory."hThe user attacks the target by dancing very hard. The user's type determines the type of this move."iThe user attacks the target by smashing into it with incredible force. It has a 20% chance to dizzy."YA full-body charge attack for slamming into the foe. The user also takes 25% recoil."mThe user attacks in an uproar, going on a rampage for two turns. Over that time, no one can fall asleep."[The user drops onto the target with its full body weight. It has a 30% chance to numb."bThe user charges the target at blinding speed. This attack always goes before any other move."jThe user bites hard on the target with its sharp front fangs. It has a 40% to make the target flinch."FThe target is slugged by a punch thrown with muscle-packed power."_A two-turn attack. Blades of wind hit the foe on the second turn. Can random critical hit."rThe user strikes with a simultaneous three-beam attack. It has a 15% chance each to numb, burn, or frostbite."bThe user slashes the target with hard and sharp claws, lowering their Defense by three steps."XAn ancient song appeals to the hearts of those listening. Switches Meloetta's form."^Seeking an opening, the user strikes continually. Ignores the target's stat step changes."ZThe target is hit with rhythmically launched punches that have a 20% chance to dizzy."kDoubles its power if the user has a status condition. Ignores damage reduction from Burn or Frostbite."dThe user sticks out its head and attacks by charging into the foe. It has a 20% chance to numb."jGets revenge for a fainted ally. If an ally fainted in the last turn, this attack's damage increases."fThe user attacks with a secret power. Its added effects vary depending on the user's environment."UThe target is attacked with a slash of claws or blades. Can random critical hit."eThis attack inflicts double damage on a numbed foe. It also cures the target's numbing, however."HThe target is jabbed with a sharply pointed horn to inflict damage."ZThe target is stomped with a big foot. It has a 30% chance to make the target flinch."hThe user approaches the target, then steals their item. Items stolen from wild Pokémon are stored."ZA unique attack that varies in type and intensity depending on the Pokémon using it."fThe user attacks with a song. Others can join in the Round and make the attack do greater damage."VStar-shaped rays are shot at the opposing team. Can't miss and skips protections."jAn attack that can be used only if the user is asleep. It has a 50% chance to make the target flinch."sUsed only if the user has no PP. Uses the higher of the user's Attack or Sp. Atk stat. It also hurts the user."mThe user attacks the foe with an echoing voice. If this move is used every turn, it does greater damage."oAn attack that hits first and makes the target flinch. It only works the first turn the user is in battle."gA restrained attack that prevents the target from fainting. The target is left with at least 1 HP."TThe user holds back when it attacks, and the target is left with at least 1 HP."]Numerous coins are hurled at the target to inflict damage. Money is earned after battle."IThe target is physically pounded with a long tail or a foreleg, etc."_Hard, pointed, and sharp claws rake the target to inflict damage. Can random critical hit."_A physical attack in which the user charges and slams into the target with its whole body."fThe user slams the target with a long tail, vines, or tentacle. The target is hit twice in a row."dAn attack that hits a target using Protect or Detect. It also lifts the effects of those moves."cA spin attack that can also eliminate trapping and hazard moves. Also raises the user's Speed."DThe target is raked two to five times. Can random critical hit."LThe user squeezes the target, trapping and damaging it for three turns."mThe target is jabbed repeatedly with a horn or beak two to five times in a row. Can random critical hit."`The user endures attacks for two turns, then strikes back to cause double the damage taken."iThe target is crushed with great force. The attack is more powerful the more HP the target has left."JAn attack move that cuts down the target's HP to equal the user's HP."bThe user flails about aimlessly to attack. It becomes more powerful the less HP the user has."bThe user throws an exploding package at enemies, or one filled with healing treats at allies."KThe user shouts with force at the target. This move always hits first."yThe power stored using the move Stockpile is released all at once in an attack. 150 base power per Stockpile charge."dThe user chomps hard on the target with its sharp front fangs. It cuts the target's HP to half."eThe user unleashes its ultimate move. Can't miss and skips protections. Only one use per battle."bThe user powerfully wrings the foe. The more HP the foe has, the greater this attack's power."NThe user helps the target and makes it use its move right after the user."bThe user hurriedly and randomly uses a move among those known by other Pokémon in the party."vThe user switches places with a party Pokémon in waiting, passing along any stat step changes. Always goes last."TThe user maximizes its Attack stat in exchange for HP equal to half its max HP."WThe user passes its held item to the target when the target isn't holding an item."NThe user blocks the target's way with arms spread wide to prevent escape."`The user tells the target a secret, lowering its Sp. Atk by three steps. Always goes first."KThe user changes its type to become the same type as one of its moves."iThe user changes its type to make itself resistant to the type of the attack the opponent used last."lThe user mimics the move used immediately before it. The move fails if no other move has been used yet."TFor four turns, this move prevents the target from using the move it last used."ZThe user compels the target to keep using only the move it last used for three turns."aThe user endures any attack with at least 1 HP. It always fails if it is used in succession."jThe user dances to compel the target to mimic it, making the target's Ability the same as the user's."RThe user focuses intensely on the fight, quadrupling its critical hit chance."VThe user draws attention to itself, making all targets take aim only at the user."GThe user intimidates the target by staring at it to cause numbing."PThe user growls, scaring nearby foes. Their Attack is lowered by two steps."_The user's body grows all at once, raising Atk and Sp. Atk by two steps, or 4 in sunshine."\The user stiffens all the muscles in its body to raise its Defense stat by three steps."`The user makes a soothing bell chime to heal the status problems of all the party Pokémon."NThe user assists an ally by boosting the power of its next attack by 50%."VThe user howls loudly to raise its Attack by three steps, and its allies' by one."^The user focuses intensely. The attack on the next turn always results in a critical hit."_The user leers at nearby foes with sharp eyes. Their Defense stat is reduced by two steps."`The user chants an incantation, preventing the foe from landing critical hits for 10 turns."hThe user tries to cut ahead of the foe to steal and use the foe's intended move with greater power."]The user pins the target with a dark, arresting look. The target becomes unable to flee."\The user waggles a finger and stimulates its brain into randomly using nearly any move."hThe user copies the move last used by the foe. The move can be used until the user is switched out."fAn attack that makes use of nature's power. Its effects vary depending on the user's environment."ZThe user intimidates all nearby foes, lowering their Attack and Sp. Atk by two steps."bThe user adds its HP to the target's HP, then equally shares the combined HP with the target."_Any Pokémon that hears this song faints in three turns, unless it switches out of battle."NIt enables the user to evade all attacks. It fails if used in succession."PThe user hypnotizes itself into copying any stat change made by the target."QRestoring its own cells, the user restores its own HP by half of its max HP."XThe user recycles a held item that has been used in battle so it can be used again."PThe user reflects the target's type, making it the same type as the target.";The user rests to cure itself of any status condition."[The foe is forced to switch out to a random ally. Always goes last. Ends wild battles."UThe user creates a protective field that prevents status problems for ten turns."\The user frightens the target with a scary face to reduce its Speed stat by four steps."UThe user's earsplitting screech reduces the target's Defense stat by four steps."KThe user edges become sharper, raising its Attack stat by three steps."~The user breaks its shell, lowering its Defense and Sp. Def by two steps but raising attacking and Speed stats by three steps."SThe user shoots a mysterious beam that changes the target's Ability to Simple."\A soothing lullaby is sung in a calming voice that puts the target into a deep slumber."jIt enables the user to permanently learn the move last used by the foe. Once used, Sketch disappears."OThe user slacks off, restoring its own HP by up to half of its maximum HP."JWhile it is asleep, the user randomly uses one of the moves it knows."BThe user restores its own HP by up to half of its maximum HP."CThe user just flops and splashes around to no effect at all..."`The user shines a spotlight on the target so that only it will be attacked during the turn."cThe user charges up power and raises both its Defense and Sp. Def. The move can be used twice."rThe user spends 25% HP to create a doll to protect it from move damage, additional affects, and status moves."PThe user generates odd sound waves from its 