 poor performance."XA Poké Ball with 4x strength against Pokémon species with 100 or more base Speed."CA Poké Ball whose strength varies with the Pokémon's weight."mA Poké Ball with 8x strength against Pokémon that are the opposite gender, but same species, as yours.":It may be held by a Pokémon to recover from numbing."8It may be held by a Pokémon to recover from sleep."9It may be held by a Pokémon to recover from poison."9It may be held by a Pokémon to recover from a burn.">It may be held by a Pokémon to recover from a frostbite."?It may be held by a Pokémon to restore a move's PP by 10."TIt may be held by a Pokémon to heal the user by 33% in a pinch (below 25% HP).">It may be held by a Pokémon to recover from being dizzy."EIt may be held by a Pokémon to recover from any status problem."BIf held by a Pokémon, it heals its HP by 25% at half health."@It may be held by a Pokémon to recover from being leeched."LWeakens a supereffective Fire-type attack against the holding Pokémon."MWeakens a supereffective Water-type attack against the holding Pokémon."PWeakens a supereffective Electric-type attack against the holding Pokémon."MWeakens a supereffective Grass-type attack against the holding Pokémon."KWeakens a supereffective Ice-type attack against the holding Pokémon."PWeakens a supereffective Fighting-type attack against the holding Pokémon."NWeakens a supereffective Poison-type attack against the holding Pokémon."NWeakens a supereffective Ground-type attack against the holding Pokémon."NWeakens a supereffective Flying-type attack against the holding Pokémon."OWeakens a supereffective Psychic-type attack against the holding Pokémon."KWeakens a supereffective Bug-type attack against the holding Pokémon."LWeakens a supereffective Rock-type attack against the holding Pokémon."MWeakens a supereffective Ghost-type attack against the holding Pokémon."NWeakens a supereffective Dragon-type attack against the holding Pokémon."LWeakens a supereffective Dark-type attack against the holding Pokémon."MWeakens a supereffective Steel-type attack against the holding Pokémon."MWeakens a supereffective Fairy-type attack against the holding Pokémon."?Weakens a Normal-type attack against the holding Pokémon."IIf held by a Pokémon, it raises its Attack by two steps in a pinch."JIf held by a Pokémon, it raises its Defense by two steps in a pinch."HIf held by a Pokémon, it raises its Speed by two steps in a pinch."JIf held by a Pokémon, it raises its Sp. Atk by two steps in a pinch."JIf held by a Pokémon, it raises its Sp. Def by two steps in a pinch."HIf held by a Pokémon, it raises its critical-hit ratio in a pinch."QIf held by a Pokémon, it raises one of its stats by three steps in a pinch."YIf held by a Pokémon, it restores its HP if it is hit by any supereffective attack."IIf held by a Pokémon, it raises its Accuracy by 4 steps in a pinch."GIf held by a Pokémon, it gets to move first just once in a pinch."[If held by a Pokémon and a physical attack hits it, the attacker takes 25% HP damage."ZIf held by a Pokémon and a special attack hits it, the attacker takes 25% HP damage."yIf held by a Pokémon, this Berry will increase the holder's Defense by four steps if it's hit with a physical move."xIf held by a Pokémon, this Berry will increase the holder's Sp. Def by four steps if it's hit with a special move."PA folding Bicycle that enables much faster movement than the Running Shoes."[A very convenient map that can be viewed anytime. It even shows your present location."dA flower sometimes bundled in bouquets to convey gratitude on special occasions like birthdays."NA ticket required to board the ship to Doxy Island. It glows beautifully.">A faded sea chart that shows the way to a certain island."iA splicer that fuses Kyurem and a certain Pokémon. They are said to have been one in the beginning."HA shiny charm which doubles the chance of finding a Shiny Pokémon."pA shiny red orb that is said to have a legend tied to it. It's known to be connected with the Hoenn region."qA shiny blue orb that is said to have a legend tied to it. It's known to be connected with the Hoenn region."jA popular treat in Lumiose City. It can be used once to heal all the status conditions of a Pokémon."kShalour City's famous shortbread. It can be used once to heal all the status conditions of a Pokémon."tThe Alola region's specialty--fried bread. It can be used once to heal all the status conditions of a Pokémon."kA capsule that allows a Pokémon with two Abilities to switch between these Abilities when it is used."qA watering can shaped like a Lotad. It helps promote the healthy growth of any Berries planted in soft soil."AA machine to fuse Necrozma, which needs light, and Solgaleo."?A machine to fuse Necrozma, which needs light, and Lunala."[An item holding Zygarde's Cores and Cells. You can use it to change Zygarde's ability."QRaises Speed sharply when a Pokémon misses with a move because of accuracy."nAn item to be held by a Pokémon. When the holder's stats are lowered, it will be switched out of battle."EThese boots prevent the effects of traps set on the battlefield."`Raises Sp. Atk by two steps when the Pokémon uses a sound move the first time each battle."_Raises Attack by two steps when the Pokémon uses a blade move the first time each battle."OA held item. The holder is protected from the negative effects of weather."hA candy that is packed with energy. When consumed, it will grant a single Pokémon 250 Exp. Points."iA candy that is packed with energy. When consumed, it will grant a single Pokémon 1000 Exp. Points."jA candy that is packed with energy. When consumed, it will grant a single Pokémon 4,000 Exp. Points."kA candy that is packed with energy. When consumed, it will grant a single Pokémon 16,000 Exp. Points."kA candy that is packed with energy. When consumed, it will grant a single Pokémon 50,000 Exp. Points."jThe fossil of an ancient Pokémon that once soared through the sky. What it looked like is a mystery."dThe fossil of an ancient Pokémon that once lived in the sea. What it looked like is a mystery."cThe fossil of an ancient Pokémon that once roamed the land. What it looked like is a mystery."yIt is said that a hero used this shield to halt a terrible disaster in ancient times. But it's grown rusty and worn."xIt is said that a hero used this sword to halt a terrible disaster in ancient times. But it's grown rusty and worn."tReins that people presented to the king. They enable Calyrex to connect and communicate with its beloved steed."tA charm that increases the Exp. Points that Pokémon can get by 10%. A machine-like object is inside the charm."AA charm that doubles the chance of getting a critical catch."OA long, durable rope. Use it to escape instantly from a cave or a dungeon."JA token which can be exchanged for a Grass-type at the Starter Store."JA token which can be exchanged for a Water-type at the Starter Store."ZA peculiar ore that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve. Associated with Arceus."IA token which can be exchanged for a Fire-type at the Starter Store."^An abandoned Dratini egg that is cold and calm. Only an expert would be able to hatch it."\An abandoned Bagon egg that is cold and calm. Only an expert would be able to hatch it."\An abandoned Gible egg that is cold and calm. Only an expert would be able to hatch it."\An abandoned Deino egg that is cold and calm. Only an expert would be able to hatch it."\An abandoned Goomy egg that is cold and calm. Only an expert would be able to hatch it."_An abandoned Jangmo-o egg that is cold and calm. Only an expert would be able to hatch it."]An abandoned Dreepy egg that is cold and calm. Only an expert would be able to hatch it."IA ticket that can be exchanged for an Eevee at the Skeevy Eevee Pub."aHeals your whole team a limited number of times. Restocked at PokeCenters and after resting."UA pack for holding medicine. If you use it, your Aid Kit will gain a max charge."RA suite of medicines. If you use it, your Aid Kit will heal more efficiently."LA stick of dynamite, perfectly suited to destroying small bits of rock."DA peculiar stone that makes certain species of Pokémon evolve."1A surf board, allowing you to surf on water."BA set of climbing gear, allowing you to climb on white rocks."SA teleporter which brings you to your last safe spot using the power of Abras."OA 3D printer which automatically copies consumed held items after battles."aIt's a cup filled with warm coffee. You probably shouldn't be keeping this in your backpack."EA package containing an important shipment destined for LuxTech."`A machine that stores excess EXP. You can activate it to turn that stored EXP into candies."BUse on a Pokémon to switch it into another one of its forms."<A suspicious package. Probably best not to look inside."KA forged ID card. It will let you pretend you work at Aegis Insurance.":A device containing evidence against Aegis Insurance."XIf reversed, gym leaders and story fights will become harder through unique curses."@Proof of ownership for the house you bought in Prizca East."jA small vial of gleaming powder. Can be used once to ensure the next wild Pokémon you find is shiny."jInfinitely mutating alien DNA. It allows a Pokémon with two abilities to switch abilities when used."QA pass that grants you access through the locked door in Victoire's factory."QA device which creates then launches regular Poké Balls, never running out."YA colorful keycard. It grants access to elevator at the Sweetrock Harbor Lighthouse.":It would be a delicious treat if you were a Pokémon."RA slip of paper with one digit of the code for the lock to Rafael's gym door."nA hi-tech recording device which increases your Pokémon's experience gained from Trainer battles by 40%."mAn upgraded, hi-tech recording device which increases the experience gained from Trainer battles by 50%."tA detailed report on how to improve as a trainer. If you decide to read it, your level cap will be raised by 5."_An ID card which unlocks Team Chasm gates and doors, giving access to dangers and rewards."aA miniature Avatar Totem. Use it to teleport to any unlocked Avatar Totems throughout Makya."?The left half of the sigil of an ancient order of knights."@The right half of the sigil of an ancient order of knights."^An ancient sigil of the Carnation Knights. You feel it pulling you towards another place."?A lump of ancient clay. It glows with a soft golden color."KA mysterious data storage device which can be used to upgrade your PC."5Unlocks the UB Containment Room at Novo Academy."JA vial of shimmering ocean water. It makes a certain Pokémon evolve."CA strange ball of light. You should gather these for a friend."?The key to the first chamber containing a powerful avatar."@The key to the second chamber containing a powerful avatar."?The key to the third chamber containing a powerful avatar."@The key to the fourth chamber containing a powerful avatar."?The key to the fifth chamber containing a powerful avatar."?The key to the sixth chamber containing a powerful avatar."AThe key to the seventh chamber containing a powerful avatar."@The key to the eighth chamber containing a powerful avatar."EA simple tree seed. It hums with the potential for great change."CMisshapen, unusual metal. Useless without a way to sharpen it."NA fragile blade of unusual metal. Sharp enough to cut alloyed overgrowth."6A thin, nearly invisible strand of unusual metal."XA charm in the shape of a tooth. It increases the EXP gained from EXP Candy by 15%."WA suite of training tools which allows you to modify your Pokémon's style points."MA key which unlocks the ruined tower on the Sandstone Estuary coastline."SHeld item which boosts move damage by 25%, but lowers the user's Speed by 15%."WA held item. At half health, the holder breaks the balloon and gains an Aqua Ring."oAn item to be held by a Pokémon. The user gets both of its legal abilities, but its stats are cut by 10%."ZRare contraband. Any average solo trainer will flee from the stench of its explosion."cA peculiar apple that can make a certain species of Pokémon evolve. It's exceptionally sweet."bA peculiar apple that can make a certain species of Pokémon evolve. It's exceptionally tart."JA key which unlocks the Ultra Beast Containment Room at Novo College."ZA flower that conveys gratitude. Use it to transform Shaymin into or out of Sky form."oAnd advanced transporter which allows you to access your Pokémon Storage to withdraw or deposit Pokémon."lA hi-tech recording device which creates a Battle Report by analyzing the results of momentuos battles."SDisables the opponent's most recently-used move for two turns upon hitting it."nCondensed essence of life. Holding it allows you to run, bike, and surf faster. Can be toggled on or off."ZA small compass. Relic of a heroic age. It can be used to find lootable items nearby."oAn electrified glove with a claw-like shape. Recovers the first failed Poké Ball thrown in a wild battle."_A comforting charm which doubles the happiness your Pokémon gain from being close to you."iA wisp of ideas with infinite potential. Use it on a Pokémon to teach any one of their legal moves."GA very tasty tail of something. It can be sold to shops for $4000."hWhen held by a Pokémon who can still evolve, reduces move damage taken by 33%. Prevents evolution."UA Pokémon held item. When the holder summons rainstorm, it lasts twice as long."eA held item. The holder recovers 30% more HP from draining moves, Ingrain, Aqua Ring, and leech."LA sinister, eerie tag that boosts the holder's Ghost-type moves by 20%."IA gleaming feather that boosts the holder's Fairy-type moves by 20%."iA spray-type medicine for wounds. It restores the HP of one Pokémon, fainted or able, by 40 points."iA spray-type medicine for wounds. It restores the HP of one Pokémon, fainted or able, by 80 points."jA spray-type medicine for wounds. It restores the HP of one Pokémon, fainted or able, by 120 points."kA spray-type medicine for wounds. It completely restores the HP of a single Pokémon, fainted or able."oA medicine that fully restores the HP and heals any status problems of a single Pokémon, fainted or able."`Very sweet chocolate. It restores the HP of one Pokémon by 40 points and makes it happier."rFried dough dipped in vanilla syrup. Heals a single Pokémon by 100 HP, and grants it 4000 Experience points."wA mentally disrupting Poké Ball that disables the Pokémon's last used move for 10 turns if it fails to catch it."LIf held by a Pokémon, it raises its Accuracy by four steps in a pinch."9A held item. The holder is protected from flinching."WA held item. The holder is protected from stat drops (except when self-inflicted)."|An ancient horn. Sound it to call 3 Pokémon to battle you. They have a higher chance of having items and unique moves."ZA vessel for negative emotions. Perfectly defeat enough trainers to earn its rewards."]If held by a Pokémon and a physical attack hits it, the attacker takes 1/4th HP damage."qA glass that reveals the truth. It is a mysterious glass that returns a Pokémon back to its original shape."eA bottle believed to have been used to seal away the power of a certain Pokémon long, long ago."kA candy that is packed with energy. When consumed, it will grant a single Pokémon 64,000 Exp. Points."GAn ancient kingly rod. You can use it to make certain plants grow."nAn advanced transporter which allows you to access your Pokémon Storage to withdraw or deposit Pokémon."[A small, versatile machine that can be used to repel wild Pokémon, or draw them near."WA high tech surveillance device. Use it to scout out the teams of nearby trainers."lA hi-tech recording device which creates a Battle Report by analyzing the results of momentous battles."_An upgraded, hi-tech recording device. It increases experience earned from battles by 10%."?A sliver of the fragment of the universe. Highly unstable.":A USB containing data from a Team Chasm's early days."hA held item. After the weilder enters a ba