e the god of this place!"9Yes, my lord. The battle is ready for your presence."3Whoa. Hadn't realized it, but I'm running dry."CGonna try to go out with a bang, but I know how this one ends."UThey don't call it the Bite Pokémon for nothing! You're stuck here with ME now!".Agnes! Rip 'em up! This is OUR arena now!"CEver been punched by a bird before? Not as funny as it sounds."8*hiss* Fine. Go, 1 Second! Don't leave him hanging!"3Oh, come ON! Turnabout's fair play, I guess..."8That's me done. Zoé, don't you let me down. Again."8I've got nothing. Nada. Bence, you better win this."8You’re close now! But don’t you dare relax yet!"MSo the lingering pain claims its first victim. Falter and you will fail!"3Delightful! It seems you've learned from this!"/Don’t give me that look. I've won worse."4NO! My friend! What have you done to my light?!"-The light! My friend's light! I NEED IT!"AGot me on the ropes, huh? Well it ain't over till it's over."#Hah. Oldest trick in the book.""Saw through my trick, did ya?"7Mystified? I've got plenty of tricks up my sleeve."(...Hope I've kept you entertained.."VWhat do you think? A little gaudy? Let me tell you: it's more than a pretty face.""Sorry. Patience is overrated."?...I've seen me win these. Yeah, I've seen me win these..."4Call me gimmicky, but I ain't a one-trick pony."	...!"...Hmph."4Tsk, tsk, tsk. It appears my work here is done.".Let's see which of you two is the better."MMy pride and joy. Don't you dare fail me now. Shred mommy's enemies, OK?"/...Dispose of this one after we’re done."8It doesn't deserve its position. You can do better."#Coup de foudre, coup de grace.">The night seems to be drawing to a close. One last dance?":All safeties disengaged - the floor is yours, Aggron."OThis is an archetypal stratagem. Do you have an effective counter planned?"'...I'm sorry. Stay down. Please..."0You’ve done enough, Artemisia. Thank you."$...It’s been so long since..."O...We’re done here. We wanted time, we got it. No need to continue this."MDon't give me that look! Don’t do it! Mavis – please, just end this."+Sleep. Rest, and awake in a new world."8The same simple pivot, again and again...I'm bored."\I suppose it would never work on you, would it? Speak my language, read me like a book."BReally? That's it? Get back up. That can't be all you've got."6I guess the power of friendship only goes so far."#Wow, that is really cathartic."OIs that all? I must've lost count. I thought we were just getting started."HYou've got a really punchable face, you know that? Smug to the end."${1} resists the pointed stones!"BAlso, critical hits are now possible on all of {1}'s attacks!":{1} firmly planted its evil roots! It can't be moved!"2The evil roots will sap foe health each turn!"%{1} is sapped by the evil roots!",\i[OMINOUSEGG]...strength in avarice..."SIt's open to a battling guide written by someone with the username "apolLyon.""1.1 Roles/Cores"2.1 Leads"3.2 Hazards"(Which entry would you like to read?"KEverything on your team needs a point. Every Pokémon needs a purpose."PIf you can't sum up its role on your team in a sentence, keep it in the PC."TEvery bit of that Pokémon should reinforce its role. Moves, items, everything."@All six Pokémon on your team need a role, narrow or broad."=Two Pokémon with synergistic roles are called a "core.""\If the two of them can take hits from a whole bunch of things, that's a defensive core."nIf together they threaten lots of Pokémon and deal with each others' counters, that's an offensive core."SCombine both and you have a balanced core. Good cores make for powerful teams."QYou don't need them, but they're a surefire way to give your team some bite."8The Pokémon you start a fight with is your "lead.""OStart every fight with it and it's a "dedicated lead." Make it a good one."@Its job is to kick things off in your favor from round one."dUsually that's by vomiting up a whole bunch of hazards. Sometimes it sets screens and explodes."kA few just try to delete whatever's on the other side, usually with short-term power boosts like Gems."FSpeaking of which, your opponent is going to have their own lead."AStop it. Taunt it, put it to sleep, or put it in the ground."IThe arena is going to very rapidly fill up with nasty pointy things."�That's because wasting a turn setting them up in the short term pays off big in the long term when they chew up a few Pokémon worth of health over the course of the match."tIf you like being alive, pack something that can clean up hazards – Defog, Terraform, or Rapid Spin, usually."uStealth Rocks are the most common hazard, so prioritize hazard removal if you've got lots of Rock-weak Pokémon."�Remember: if your favorite little gremlin is switching out nine times a match or is cripplingly weak to funny pebbles, put Heavy-Duty Boots on it." They're cute and effective."Unknown Map."You exit the PC."VIt's open to a battling guide written by someone with the username "snowwhip401.""Even keel"Best foot forward"Rolling with the punches"<All the little pieces of your team need their own role."dUse whatever you want; just ensure that it's got something to do and the best odds of doing it."5Give bulky Pokémon Leftovers and healing moves."IGive strong, slow Pokémon Focus Sashes, Vests, or ways to speed up."You get the idea."aIf you can, try to have all kinds of Pokémon on your team, so you have answers to anything."pPhysical and special bulk and power, type matchups, speed profiles – a diverse team is a diverse toolbox."ISend out the Pokémon that helps everything else on your team first.":If you have a weather or a Room to set up, get to it."EIf you don't have a clear, clean gameplan, ruin your opponent's."wA dedicated lead's worst fear is usually a strong multi-hitting move. Neither Sturdy nor Sash can help them there."}As opposed to simply trading hazards, outspeeding and KOing a lead before it gets going can give you an early advantage."8Each Pokémon's utility is defined by the opponent."ZIf your opponent has several Fire-type Pokémon, your Primarina is far more valuable."0Conserve its health and leverage its power."]In the same match, an Aegislash may be far less valuable – be willing to sacrifice it."ZThere's no shame in letting a Pokémon fall in order to get a safe switch to another."xWhile they may seem drastic, moves such as Healing Wish or Explosion can turn the tide of a match in a single turn."kFainting the user can, if used with finesse, be an advantage – think of them as the ultimate U-Turn."ABut it failed, since the target didn't choose to use a move!"@But it failed, since the target chose to use a status move!"GBut it failed, since the target chose a move that can't be copied!"PBut it failed, since #{user.pbThis(true)} knows no other sound-based moves!"*{1} is jealous of {2}'s good fortune!"{1} is wary of the ground!"{1} gathers toxic gas!"*{1} is warming up its haunting voice!"${1} is winding up a big attack!"{1} takes its vengeance!"({1} prevents a random added effect!"{1} grows one size bigger!"{1} is fully grown!"{1} also heals {2}!"2For {1} to have two items, both must be Gems!"5For {1} to have two items, both must be Berries!"3For {1} to have two items, both must be Herbs!">For {1} to have two items, at least one must be Clothing!"9For {1} to have two items, only one can be Clothing!"/{1} catches the full force of {2}'s Speed!" Which item should {1} drop?"#{1} can switch out regardless!"){1} is blessed by the shattered sky!"?Time is dancing to {1}'s tune! This turn is being skipped!"The {1} stayed the same."The {1} was refreshed!"#It'll last for {1} more turns."O{1} cannot use any of its moves, and will Struggle if it fights. Go ahead?"-{1} must use {2} if it fights. Go ahead?"+{1} slurped up venom leaking from {2}."({1}'s team takes joy in {2}'s pain!"/Its allied {1} was revived to full health!"{1} can't hold a {2}!")But {1} hold's tightly onto its {2}!"{1} showed mercy on {2}!"2{1} would have flinched, but it's immune now!";{1} wou